	}>>
	<<set $hcChallengesRun to []>>
<</if>>

<<speechresolve>>
<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"Um, Winter?" you ask, raising your hand. "Before you start, are there any other details to this story, in other variations?"
	<br><br>
	Your hand falls back to your lap the moment <<he>> looks your way.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"Um, Winter?" you ask, raising your hand. "Before you start, are there any other details to this story, in other variations?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"Winter," you say, careful not to interrupt too sharply. "Before you begin, are there any less common details or variations worth mentioning?"
	<br><br>
	You give the painting another glance, trying to sound curious rather than impatient.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"I've sat through this story so many times," you huff. "The first times you told it, you left out details. Anything like that you could throw in?"
	<br><br>
	Winter gives you a long look. You shrug, refusing to soften the question.
<<else>>
	"Are there any other variations to this story that haven't been covered yet?" you ask. "Details not widely agreed upon, or anything like that."
	<br><br>
	You sit back after asking, listening for anything Winter skipped.
<</if>>
<br><br>

Winter pauses, thinking. "Well, there are a few aspects some tellings disagree on. For the most part, I've tried to stick to the most accepted versions, but..."
<<He>> smiles. "Alright. I'll try to include some more niche aspects. Was there anything you had in mind? As a jumping-off point."
<br><br>

