/* Event start */
:: Hopeless Cycle
<<hopelessCycleStart>>
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<canvas-model-override "mouth" "neutral">>
<span class="narration">
It's generally agreed upon that the event took place late in the 14th century.
The Cloister of Virgo, as they called themselves, held much control over the region.
<br><br>

This comes some years after a religious conflict that nearly spelled their annihilation.
Persecution was common, as they were eager to punish any they deemed guilty of having a hand in the conflict.
Or their descendants.
</span>
<br><br>

It's rarely quiet in the temple's dungeon, but when it is, it's deafening.
<br><br>

One thing that never fails to inspire instant silence is the reverberation of heavy boots on stone.
There's only one pair of boots in the whole faith heavy enough to make that specific dirge,
and only one bastard big enough to wear them.
<br><br>

You lean forward in your plain wooden chair, counting the footsteps. Only one pair.
That means <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>>'s alone, and thus probably here to yell at you.
You put your book down and brace yourself as the light of <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> torch begins to leak into the guardhouse.
The other gaolers all stand at attention. You don't bother. It's never made a difference with <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>.
<br><br>

<<worldMale 'His' 'Her'>> massive frame finally comes into view, along with <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> ugly brown-bearded face, marred with a lopsided handprint branding. An absolute wall of a <<worldMale 'man' 'woman'>>. The Bishop's Hand. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>>'s carrying something over <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> shoulder. A long, limp sack, split at the bottom into two-
no, that's a person. <<worldMale 'His' 'Her'>> dark eyes scan the room, passing each guard, until <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> eyes land on you. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> holds <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> torch out wordlessly.
<br><br>

<<link [[Take the torch|Hopeless Cycle Torch]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Make <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> carry it <<worldMale 'himself' 'herself'>>|Hopeless Cycle Torch]]>><<hcSuspicion 2>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Offer to carry the new prisoner instead|Hopeless Cycle Torch]]>><<set $prisoner.love += 1>><<set $phase to 3>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Torch
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<span class="narration">
There are many versions of this tale, but there are some constants across all of them.
The first of which is that the Bishop's Hand was a cruel, vicious enforcer.
<br><br>

Where the stories diverge depends on whether <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> was the exception, or the norm.
The wounds were still fresh. The Cloister's vengeance, swift and terrible. It inspired cruelty in many.
</span>
<br><br>

<<if $phase is 1>>
	<<wearProp "torch">>
	You take the outstretched torch, as is expected of you.
<<elseif $phase is 2>>
	You do nothing. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> growls, before handing it out to someone else. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> grabs your tunic and yanks you forward in front of <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>. Looks like you're not getting out of this one.
<<else>>
	<<wearProp "torch">>
	You outstretch your arms towards the prisoner. The Bishop's Hand makes an amused grunt, but hits you on the forehead with the handle of the torch, before holding it out again. You take the hint this time. <<pain 2>><<gpain>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> nods towards the limp figure over <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> shoulder. "Fresh from the wall." <<worldMale 'His' 'Her'>> voice is a lecherous rumble, making the following belly laugh all the more unsettling. "Hounds enjoyed their meat."
<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> points forward, down the primary corridor. <<if $phase isnot 2>>You light the way forward.<<else>>The other guard lights the way forward, and you follow.<</if>>
<br><br>

One. Two. Three. Four. Five. Six. Seven. Eight. Nine. Ten. Nine. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> stops to think. Eight. Nine. Ten. Nine. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> finally stops on the ninth cell. Only five of the cells you passed were even occupied.
You expertly find the right key on your key ring, unlocking the cell. <<if $phase is 2>><<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> shoves you in ahead of <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>><<else>>You enter ahead of <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>><</if>>.
<br><br>

<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> approaches the back wall, laying the new prisoner down. "You won't get much noise out of this one," <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> says as <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> secures <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> silver manacles to the wall by a chain. "No more singing for this birdie."
<br><br>

<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> turns to you, chuckling. Staring. As if waiting for you to speak out of turn.
<br><br>

<<link [[Ask what <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> crimes are|Hopeless Cycle Ask]]>><<hcSuspicion 5>><<set $prisoner.love += 1>><<set $phase2 to 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Stay silent|Hopeless Cycle Ask]]>><<set $phase2 to 2>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask what your orders are|Hopeless Cycle Ask]]>><<hcSuspicion -3>><<set $phase2 to 3>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Ask
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<span class="narration">
Every spin on this tale, every divergence, comes from this <<worldMale 'man' 'woman'>>. <<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> personal gaoler.
<<worldMale 'His' 'Her'>> name is lost to time, but most sources point to <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> being a member of the old Fayne noble family.
A family with deep, historic ties to the cloister. It's probable that many of <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> in worship were familial as well.
</span>
<br><br>

<<if $phase2 is 1>>
	You ask why <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>>'s being locked up. Immediately, <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> punches you in the gut, doubling you over. <<pain 6>><<ggpain>>
	<br><br>

	"You know better than to ask. You wait for me to tell you, if I think you need to know."
<<elseif $phase2 is 2>>
	You stay quiet. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> makes a satisfied grunt.
<<else>>
	You obediently ask for your orders. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> gruffs under <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> breath. "Such a good dog, always ready to heel."
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> removes a pouch from <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> waist, and draws a big cross on the wall in dark grey paste. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> speaks as <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> works.
<br><br>

"<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>>'s a witch. Consorted with the Dark Elk and seduced the townsfolk. They're not happy about <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> being taken." <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> walks to the next wall and starts the second cross. "Ungrateful pigs."
<br><br>

<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> finishes the cross, moving to the third wall. "<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>>'s your responsibility. Personally. Too much of a contamination risk for more than one guard, which means you don't touch any other prisoners." <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> pauses to point at you. <span class="blue">"It also means you get sanctified whenever you enter or leave the dungeon."</span>
<br><br>

<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> finishes the last cross. "<span class="red">Make sure <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> lives, but hates every minute of it.</span> Bring <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> salvation through suffering. <span class="blue">Be here every day, at mid-day, for <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> penance.</span> Keep <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> intact until the red moon. <span class="red">If you show mercy, I'll assume <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> bewitched you.</span>" <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> pushes past you, <<if $phase is 2>>leaving with the other guard<<else>>yanking the torch from your hands and leaving the cell<</if>>. You're plunged into darkness.
<br><br>

The cell's too dark for you to even inspect <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> now. You'll need to grab another torch.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Cell]]>><<endevent>><<set $hc.daily.enteredDungeon to true>><</link>>
<br>

/* Dungeon / guardhouse */
:: Hopeless Cycle Dungeon
<<set $location to "old_temple">><<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $bus to "guardhouse">>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

You are in the guardhouse of the temple's dungeon. There are several hallways, each housing ten cells.
<<if ["dusk","night"].includes(Time.dayState) and $hc.dungeonTorchState isnot "lit">>
	<<if hcItemLitTorch()>>
		<span class="orange">Your torch lights up the gloom.</span>
	<<else>>
		It's dark and silent.
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if $hc.dungeonTorchTime lte 0>>
		<<if Time.dayState is "dawn">>
			It's always brightest at dawn, as the rising sun's light hits this part of the temple directly.
		<<else>>
			A small amount of light trickles in from upstairs, and through tiny barred windows.
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		Torchlight flickers along the walls.
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
	Rain slowly seeps in through the windows, trickling down the gentle slope of each hall into a drain at the centre.
<</if>>
There's a stairway to the disposal channel here.
<br>
<<if $hc.intro>>
	<<if $hc.dungeonTorchState is "lit" and $hc.dungeonTorchTime gte 1>>
		<span class="orange">The torches will burn for <span class="gold"><<number $hc.dungeonTorchTime>></span> more <<pluralise $hc.dungeonTorchTime "hour">>, unless snuffed.</span>
		<<if ["dusk","night"].includes(Time.dayState)>>
			<<if Time.dayState is "dusk">>
				<span class="blue">You're expected to snuff them come nightfall.</span>
			<<else>>
				<span class="red">It's past nightfall. They may arouse suspicion.</span>
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		<<if $hc.dungeonTorchState is "snuffed" and $hc.dungeonTorchTime gte 1>>
			<span class="blue">The torches have been snuffed. When re-ignited, they will burn for <span class="gold"><<number $hc.dungeonTorchTime>></span> <<pluralise $hc.dungeonTorchTime "hour">>.</span>
			<<if hcItemLitTorch()>>
				Re-ignition will be easy, as you already have some fire.
			<<else>>
				Re-ignition will be slow and tedious without a lit torch on-hand.
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<set $hc.dungeonTorchState to "burnt">>
			<span class="red">The torches have all burned out.</span> They will take time and effort to fully replace.
		<</if>>
		<<if !["dusk","night"].includes(Time.dayState)>>
			<<if Time.hour gte 12>>
				<span class="red">You were expected to have lit them by now!</span>
			<<else>>
				<span class="yellow">You're expected to light them by mid-day.</span>
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<<if $hc.handLocation is "guardhouse">>
		<<set $hc.daily.handWarning to true>>
		<br>
		<span class="red">The Bishop's Hand is here, inspecting and harrowing prisoners.</span>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<br>

<<if _hcEvent is "blood">>
	The heavy dirge of footsteps comes down the dungeon stairs. "<span class="red">It's time, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>.</span> Bring the witch up at once."
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Enter <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell|Hopeless Cycle Blood Cell]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $stress gte $stressmax>>
	<<hopelessCyclePassout>>
<<elseif $hc.suspicion gte 100>>
	<span class="red">Everything goes dark as a sack is pulled over your head.</span> You're quickly struck in the gut, doubling you over. You're forced to your knees.
	<br><br>

	The last thing you feel is an impact against your head.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Ending E]]>><<pass 4 hours>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif (Time.hour gte 23 or Time.hour lte 4) and ($hc.nightBreakIn is "tonight" or $hc.nightBreakIn is "heard")>>
	<<loadNPC 0 "hc_abuser">><<person1>>
	You hear faint footsteps down one of the cell halls. <span class="red">You look, and see the door to <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell open.</span> You place your hand on your $temple_weapon.
	<br><br>

	You slowly approach, and hear a voice. "Wretched <<worldFemale 'seductress' 'seducer'>>," a <<personssimple>> voice spits. "Why should <<worldMale 'Brother' 'Sister'>> Fayne have you to <<worldMale 'himself' 'herself'>>? My vows are already broken. I may as well..."
	<br><br>

	You peek into the cell, and see a <<personsimple>> in black robes approaching <<print $prisoner.name>>.
	<<if $hcChallenge.faithBlooms>>
		<<His>> fingers twitch. "Do you remember these hands? <span @class="$prisonerEvents.includes('washHair') ? 'red' : ''">They took your hair so easily.</span> I'll be <i>taking</i> more than just a lock of hair this time."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Sneak out of the dungeon|Hopeless Cycle Cell Caught Sneak]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Intervene|Hopeless Cycle Cell Caught Intervene]]>><<set $prisoner.love += 10>><</link>><<hopelessCycleLove 2>>
	<br>
<<elseif _hcEvent is "dailyPunishment">>
	The Bishop's Hand stands by <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell with a confessor. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> waves you over. "It's time, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>."
	<br><br>

	You enter the cell with <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>.
	<br><br>

	<<if $hc.gameOver>>
		<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Ending F]]>><<endevent>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Prisoner Inspection]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if !$hc.intro>>
		One of the other gaolers is waving you over.
		<br>
		<<socialiseicon>><<link [[Approach and talk (0:05)|Hopeless Cycle Friend]]>><<set $hc.intro to true>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<switch $hc.dungeonTorchState>>
			<<case "burnt">>
				<<if !["night"].includes(Time.dayState) or hcItemLitTorch()>>
					<<link [[Replace torches <<hcTimeTaskDisplay 150>>|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon Torch]]>><<set $torchAction to "dungeonTorchReplace">><<hcTimeTaskPass 150>><<tiredness 6>><<set $hc.dungeonTorchTime to 11>><<set $hc.dungeonTorchState to "snuffed">><</link>><<gtiredness>>
				<<else>>
					<span class="red">It's too dark to replace the torches. You'll have to wait until daybreak, or get light from elsewhere.</span>
				<</if>>
			<<case "snuffed">>
				<<if hcItemLitTorch()>>
					<<link [[Re-ignite torches <<hcTimeTaskDisplay 10>>|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon Torch]]>><<set $torchAction to "dungeonTorchReignite">><<hcTimeTaskPass 10>><<set $hc.dungeonTorchState to "lit">><</link>>
				<<elseif !["night"].includes(Time.dayState)>>
					<<if hcItemHolding("torch")>>
						<<link [[Light a torch by hand (0:15)|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon Torch]]>><<set $torchAction to "dungeonTorchByHand">><<pass 15>><<tiredness 12>><<set hcItemHolding("torch").state to "lit">><<set hcItemHolding("torch").time to $hcChallenge.torchFaster ? 10 : 5>><</link>><<ggtiredness>>
					<<else>>
						<span class="blue">Grab a snuffed torch to light it by hand.</span>
					<</if>>
				<<else>>
					<span class="red">It's too dark to light a torch by hand. You'll have to wait until daybreak, or get light from elsewhere.</span>
				<</if>>
				<<if $hc.dungeonTorchTime lt 6>>
					<br>
					<<link [[Renew torch fuel <<hcTimeTaskDisplay 30>>|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon Torch]]>><<set $torchAction to "dungeonTorchRenew">><<hcTimeTaskPass 30>><<set $hc.dungeonTorchTime += 8>><</link>>
				<</if>>
			<<default>>
				<<if hcItemCanReach("snuffer")>>
					<<link [[Snuff torches <<hcTimeTaskDisplay 10>>|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon Torch]]>><<set $torchAction to "dungeonTorchSnuff">><<set $hc.dungeonTorchState to "snuffed">><<hcTimeTaskPass 10>><</link>>
				<<else>>
					<span class="red">You need your torch cap to snuff the torches.</span>
				<</if>>
		<</switch>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<br>

	<<set _itemsHere.push("torch")>>
	<div id="hcItems" class="no-numberify"><<hopelessCycleItemLinks>></div>

	<b><u>Locations:</u></b><br>
	<<if $hc.gameOver>>
		<span class="red">...</span><br>
		<<prisonicon "cell">><<link [[Enter <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell|Hopeless Cycle Ending F]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<<elseif $hc.nightBreakIn is "failed">>
		<<prisonicon "cell">><<link [[Enter <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell|Hopeless Cycle Night Break In Aftermath]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<<prisonicon "cell">><<link [[Enter <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell|Hopeless Cycle Cell]]>><<endevent>><<set $hcAction to "enter">><</link>>
	<</if>>
	<br>

	<<if $hc.intro>>
		<<if Time.dayState is "night" and (Time.hour gte 23 or Time.hour lte 5)>>
			<<if $worn.upper.name is "chain tunic" or hcItemLitTorch()>>
				<<if $worn.upper.name is "chain tunic">>
					<span class="red">Your armour makes you conspicuous.</span>
				<</if>>
				<<if hcItemLitTorch()>>
					<span class="red">Your lit torch will make sneaking impossible.</span>
				<</if>>
				<br>
			<</if>>
			<<getouticon>><<link [[Sneak out to the cloister (0:02)|Hopeless Cycle Cloister Sneak]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
			<br>
		<<else>>
			<<templeicon "cloister">><<link [[Cloister <<hcTimeDungeonDisplay>>|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon Leave]]>><<hcTimeDungeonPass>><</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<if hcItemLitTorch()>>
			<<sewericon "main">><<link [[Disposal channel (0:05)|Hopeless Cycle Disposal]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<<elseif $hcItems.some(torch => torch.type is "torch" and torch.location is "disposal" and torch.inSconce is true and torch.state is "lit")>>
			<<sewericon "main">><<link [[Disposal channel (0:05)|Hopeless Cycle Disposal]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<<else>>
			<span class="red">The disposal channel is too dark to enter without a torch.</span>
		<</if>>
		<br>
	<</if>>

	<<if $debug is 1>>
		<br>
		<<hcicon "bucket">><<link [[Item debugging|Hopeless Cycle Debug]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Friend
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<generateTemple 1>><<person1>>
<span class="narration">When faced with a common trouble, such as a sadistic taskmaster, it was easy to form bonds with those standing beside <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>.</span>
<br><br>

<<He>> pats you on the shoulder.
<<if $pain gte 20>>
	"<<worldMale 'King' 'Queen'>> shit-beard didn't rough you up too badly, did <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>>?" <<He>> cleans off your face with a piece of damp cloth. <<pain -10>><<llpain>>
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	"Looks like <<worldMale 'king' 'queen'>> shit-beard has it out for you." <<He>> chuckles under <<his>> breath.
<</if>>
"We're in this together, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>. Remember who the real enemy is." <<He>> shoots a sharp glare at <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell. "Give <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> a few extra lashes for me."
<br><br>

<<He>> starts to leave the dungeon, but pauses on the first step. <span class="blue">"Don't forget to snuff the torches when you're done here for the night."</span>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Dungeon Torch
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<switch $torchAction>>
	<<case "dungeonTorchReplace">>
		<<run hcItemAdd("torch", "disposal")>>
		<<run hcItemAdd("torch", "disposal")>>
		<<run hcItemAdd("torch", "disposal")>>
		You open every bolted sconce, collect every useless torch, and toss them down the disposal channel stairs. Most of them should roll into water by themselves. You hope.
		<br><br>

		You painstakingly prepare dozens of torches for use. Each one is a process. Haft. Animal fat. Kindling. Fabric. Pitch. Repeat. Haft. Fat. Kindling. Fabric. Pitch...
		<br><br>

		It takes you a long time. When you finally place the last torch in its sconce, you wipe your brow in satisfaction. <<trauma -12>><<lltrauma>>
		<br><br>

		You remember that you still need to light them. <<stress 3>><<gstress>>
	<<case "dungeonTorchReignite">>
		You walk down each hall, meticulously lighting every torch. <<trauma -3>><<ltrauma>>
	<<case "dungeonTorchRenew">>
		You add more animal fat, fabric and pitch to each torch, ensuring they don't burn to the haft. It takes a while, but it's nowhere near as bad as preparing around three-dozen new torches from scratch. <<trauma -6>><<ltrauma>>
	<<case "dungeonTorchByHand">>
		Haft. Animal fat. Kindling. Fabric. Pitch. You wave your unlit torch around to make sure nothing comes loose. It all holds together well. You've done this hundreds of times by now, so you're quite good at it.
		<br><br>

		That doesn't make it any less tedious. You grab a handful of kindling, and an unused haft. You twirl it between your hands until you see smoke, then blow into it.
		<br><br>

		You stick the end of your torch in, and finally have a light.
	<<case "dungeonTorchSnuff">>
		<<wearProp "antique snuffer">>
		<<if hcItemHolding("snuffer")>>
			You twirl your torch cap idly for a moment.
		<<else>>
			You grab your torch cap from the wall.
		<</if>>
		It's a bell-shaped metal cup on a small, bent rod. You place it over the first torch, starving it of air and quickly putting it out. You walk down each hallway, repeating the process.
		<br><br>

		You've always found this oddly satisfying. <<stress -6>><<lstress>>
<</switch>>
<br><br>

<<unset $torchAction>>
<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Dungeon Leave
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<set _susFromContainers to 0>>

<<run $hcItems.filter(containers => containers.containerID &&
	containers.location === "held" &&
	!V.hcItems.some(thing => thing.type === "sheets" && thing.location === containers.containerID)).forEach(container => {
	V.hcItems.filter(item => item.location === container.containerID && ["clothes", "snuffer", "bandages", "food", "clutter", "bones"].includes(item.type)).forEach(gip => {
		T.susFromContainers++;
	})
})>>
<<generateTemple 1>><<person1>>
<<if $exposed gte 2>>
	You leave the dungeon. A <<priest>> awaits you at the top of the stairs, and covers <<his>> mouth when <<he>> notices your exposure. "<<worldMale 'Brother' 'Sister'>>, what happened?"
	<br><br>

	You're forced to stay there, exposed, for an agonisingly long time as you undergo the prayers and blessings. <<stress 40>><<gggstress>><<trauma 50>><<gggtrauma>><<hcSuspicion 10>><<hopelessCycleSus 2>>
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	<<if !$hc.daily.enteredDungeon>>
		<<if $worn.upper.name isnot "chain tunic">>
			You leave the dungeon. A <<priest>> awaits you at the top of the stairs, and looks confused. "<<worldMale 'Brother' 'Sister'>>? I never saw you enter. Where is your armour?" You undergo the lengthy process of prayers and blessings to purge the witch's filth from your body. <<stress 8>><<gstress>><<trauma 10>><<gtrauma>><<hcSuspicion 20>><<hopelessCycleSus 3>>
		<<else>>
			You leave the dungeon. A <<priest>> awaits you at the top of the stairs, and looks confused. "<<worldMale 'Brother' 'Sister'>>? I never saw you enter." You undergo the lengthy process of prayers and blessings to purge the witch's filth from your body. <<stress 8>><<gstress>><<trauma 10>><<gtrauma>><<hcSuspicion 10>><<hopelessCycleSus 2>>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		You leave the dungeon. A <<priest>> awaits you at the top of the stairs. You undergo the lengthy process of prayers and blessings to purge the witch's filth from your body. <<stress 8>><<gstress>><<trauma 10>><<gtrauma>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<if _susFromContainers>>
		<<Hes>> too busy with the rites to inspect the items in your bucket, but some of your other <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> steal the occasional glance. <<hcSuspicion _susFromContainers>><<hopelessCycleSus 1>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Cloister]]>><<endevent>><<set $hc.daily.enteredDungeon to false>><<set $hc.snuckInDungeon to false>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Dungeon Enter
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
/* Items that are suspicious when held inside containers, unless that container also holds a bedsheet */
<<set _susFromContainers to 0>>
<<run $hcItems.filter(containers => containers.containerID &&
	containers.location === "held" &&
	!V.hcItems.some(thing => thing.type === "sheets" && thing.location === containers.containerID)).forEach(container => {
	V.hcItems.filter(item => item.location === container.containerID && ["clothes", "snuffer", "bandages", "food", "clutter", "bones"].includes(item.type)).forEach(gip => {
		T.susFromContainers++;
	})
})>>

<<generateTemple 1>><<person1>>
You approach the stairs to the dungeon.
<<if $worn.upper.name isnot "chain tunic">>
	A <<priest>> awaits you, and raises <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> hand to stop you. "<<worldMale 'Brother' 'Sister'>>, I can't let you in without your armour. It's an important part of the sanctification."
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Cloister]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<if $hc.daily.enteredDungeon>>
		A <<priest>> awaits you, and raises an eyebrow. "<<worldMale 'Brother' 'Sister'>>? I didn't see you leave." You undergo the lengthy process of prayers and blessings to ready yourself for exposure to the witch. <<stress 8>><<gstress>><<trauma 10>><<gtrauma>> <<hcSuspicion 10>><<hopelessCycleSus 2>>
	<<else>>
		A <<priest>> awaits you. You undergo the lengthy process of prayers and blessings to ready yourself for exposure to the witch. <<stress 8>><<gstress>><<trauma 10>><<gtrauma>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<if _susFromContainers>>
		<<Hes>> too busy with the rites to inspect the items in your bucket, but some of your other <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> steal the occasional glance. <<hcSuspicion _susFromContainers>><<hopelessCycleSus 1>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon]]>><<endevent>><<hcTimeDungeonPass>><<set $hc.daily.enteredDungeon to true>><<set $hc.snuckInDungeon to false>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Cloister Sneak
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

You sneak back to the cloister.
<<if $worn.upper.name is "chain tunic">>
	<span class="red">Your noisy chain armour does not make it easy. Someone certainly heard you.</span> <<hcSuspicion 10>><<hopelessCycleSus 2>>
<<elseif hcItemLitTorch()>>
	<span class="red">A lit torch makes for poor stealth, however. It's likely someone saw you.</span> <<hcSuspicion 10>><<hopelessCycleSus 2>>
<<else>>
	You don't think anyone heard or saw you.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Cloister]]>><<set $hc.snuckInDungeon to false>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Dungeon Sneak
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

You sneak into the dungeon from the cloister.
<<if $worn.upper.name is "chain tunic">>
	<span class="red">Your noisy chain armour does not make it easy. Someone certainly heard you.</span> <<hcSuspicion 10>><<hopelessCycleSus 2>>
<<elseif hcItemLitTorch()>>
	<span class="red">A lit torch makes for poor stealth, however. It's likely someone saw you.</span> <<hcSuspicion 10>><<hopelessCycleSus 2>>
<<else>>
	You don't think anyone heard or saw you.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon]]>><<set $hc.snuckInDungeon to true>><</link>>
<br>


/* Disposal channel */
:: Hopeless Cycle Disposal
<<set $location to "drain">><<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $bus to "disposal">>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<set _torchInSconce to $hcItems.find(torch => torch.type is "torch" and torch.state is "lit" and torch.location is "disposal" and torch.inSconce is true)>>

You are in the temple's disposal channel, a labyrinth of stone and rushing waterways. You're told it doesn't connect to the fresh water cisterns.
A long stone staircase connects it to the temple's dungeon.
<br><br>

<<if $exposed gte 2>>
	You feel wretched, being exposed around such filth. <<stress 20>><<ggstress>><<trauma 6>><<gtrauma>>
<<else>>
	You've always hated this place, ever since you were an initiate. <<trauma 2>><<gtrauma>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if $stress gte $stressmax>>
	<<hopelessCyclePassout>>
<<elseif !hcItemLitTorch() and !_torchInSconce>>
	<<if !$hc.disposalDarkCount>>
		<<set $hc.disposalDarkCount to 0>>
	<</if>>
	<span class="red">It's pitch black. You can't see where you're going!</span>
	<br><br>

	<<cleareventpool>>
	<<addinlineevent "dungeon">>
		<<set _toDrop to $hcItems.find(bucket => bucket.name is "bucket" and bucket.location is "held")>>
		<<if _toDrop>>
			<<set _toDrop.location to "disposal">>
			<span class="red">You drop your held bucket!</span> You fumble around for it, but it's no use. You'll have to come back and look for it with a light source.
			<br><br>

			After much more stumbling around, you finally find your way to a staircase.
			<br><br>

			<<prisonicon "cell">><<link [[Dungeon (0:20)|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon]]>><<pass 20>><</link>>
			<br>
		<<else>>
			After some stumbling around, you find your way to a staircase.
			<br><br>

			<<prisonicon "cell">><<link [[Dungeon (0:20)|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon]]>><<pass 20>><</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "lizard">>
		<<beastNEWinit 1 lizard>>
		A massive <<beasttype>> rears out of the water! There's something unnatural about <<bhim>>, other than <<bhis>> size. There's something protruding from <<bhis>> brow ridge, almost like tree branches.
		<br><br>

		<<if ($monster is 1 or $settings.bestialityEnabled) and not ($NPCList[0] and $NPCList[0].lewdBlocked)>>
			<<bHes>> on you in an instant.
			<br><br>

			<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Lizard]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>><</link>>
			<br>
		<<else>>
			You manage to struggle free, but not unscathed. <<beastescape>>
			<br><br>

			You eventually find a staircase after much more blind stumbling.
			<br><br>

			<<prisonicon "cell">><<link [[Dungeon (0:20)|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon]]>><<pass 20>><</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<if $hc.disposalDarkCount gte 3 or !$hcChallenge.forestNoShortcut or $hc.shortcutCount gte 1>>
		<<if $hc.disposalDarkCount gte 3 and !$hc.forestPassage>>
			<<set _forcedPassage to true>>
			<<cleareventpool>>
		<</if>>
		<<addinlineevent "forest">>
			Your hands press against something hard and cold. You push, and it clatters to the ground noisily. You see light further beyond.
			<br><br>

			You feel the ground start to slope. It feels like you're walking upwards now.
			<br><br>

			You emerge in the forest.
			<br><br>

			<<if $hc.shortcutCount isnot undefined and !_forcedPassage>>
				<<set $hc.shortcutCount to 0>>
				You feel a pair of eyes watching you, and hear a piercing screech of glass rubbing against glass. <span class="red">You no longer have permission to travel this path,</span> and must make another offering if you wish to pass.
			<</if>>

			<<foresticon>><<link [[Forest (0:20)|Hopeless Cycle Forest]]>><<pass 20>><<set $hcForest to 15>><<set $hc.forestPassage to true>><</link>>
			<br>
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>

	<<runeventpool>>
	<<set $hc.disposalDarkCount++>>
<<else>>
	<<if !$hc.disposalState and $hc.disposals gte 5>>
		<<set $hc.disposalState to 1>>
		You hear something like glass scraping against stone in the distance. <<stress 6>><<gstress>>
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Disposal]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<elseif $hc.disposalState is 1 and $hc.disposals gte 15>>
		<<set $hc.disposalState to 2>>
		You hear a rapid rattling and thumping approach from the darkness.
		<<if hcItemLitTorch()>>
			You swing your torch in its direction, but see nothing.
		<<else>>
			You quickly retreat to the light of the torch. You look around, but see nothing.
		<</if>>
		The light seems much more extreme. Within is much brighter, yet everything outside is somehow even darker than it was before.
		<<stress 24>><<ggstress>>
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Disposal]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<elseif $hc.disposalState is 2 and $hc.disposals gte 20>>
		<<set $hc.disposalState to 3>>
		You hear the rapid thumping approach again, followed by the scraping of glass on stone. It's loud, and very close. You take a few steps back, until you hit the wall.
		<br><br>

		<span class="red">You feel a breath on the top of your head.</span><<stress 24>><<ggstress>>
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Don't look|Hopeless Cycle Disposal Torch Friend]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>><<willpowerdifficulty 400 900>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Look|Hopeless Cycle Disposal Torch Friend]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<elseif $hc.disposalState is 3 and $hc.disposals gte 30 and $hc.glassfingers>>
		<<set $hc.disposalState to 4>>
		You turn away from the disposal channel, and see your own reflection.
		<br><br>

		A humanoid figure, entirely reflective and featureless save for a pair of beady yellow eyes and a cracked smile, sits before you. It's at your eye level despite sitting down. Its mere presence is devouring the light.
		<br><br>

		It opens its fissure-shaped mouth, revealing an impossibly long yellow tongue wrapped around something. Light pours from its throat. Its tongue extends and unfurls until it's right in front of you, revealing something strange, and terribly pale.
		<br><br>

		<span class="red">The bones of a human wrist and forearm.</span> The tongue flicks, as if motioning for you to take them. You hesitantly do so.
		<br><br>

		The reflective creature's tongue retracts and its mouth slams shut, sealing its surface once more. It's no longer reflective, now being translucent.
		<br><br>

		It turns, getting on all fours and skittering away with disturbing speed for its size.
		<br><br>

		You remember a short rhyme from when you were a child.<br>
		<i>If ever your heart a wish to make,<br>
		In your hands the wishing stones,<br>
		Cast upon the holy lake,<br>
		In their absence, clutching bones.</i>
		<br><br>

		<<run hcItemAdd({ type: "bones", name: "forearm bones", location: "held", origin: "wraith" })>>

		<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Disposal]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<if $hc.forestPassage and $hc.shortcutCount isnot undefined>>
			<<if $hc.shortcutCount gt 1>>
				You feel you have permission to take the shortcut to the forest <span class="blue"><<number $hc.shortcutCount>></span> more times.
			<<elseif $hc.shortcutCount is 1>>
				You feel you have permission to take the shortcut to the forest <span class="blue">one</span> more time.
				<span class="pink">You would not be able to return here. It would be a one way trip.</span>
			<<else>>
				You feel you <span class="red">do not have permission</span> to take the shortcut to the forest.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
		<div id="hcItems" class="no-numberify"><<hopelessCycleItemLinks>></div>

		<b><u>Locations:</u></b><br>
		<<prisonicon "cell">><<link [[Dungeon (0:05)|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<if $hc.forestPassage>>
			<<if hcItemLitTorch()>>
				<<if $hcChallenge.forestNoShortcut and !$hc.shortcutCount>>
					<<foresticon>><<link [[Passage to forest (0:20)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
				<<else>>
					<<foresticon>><<link [[Passage to forest (0:20)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut]]>><<pass 20>><<set $hcForest to 15>><<set $hc.snuckInDungeon to false>><</link>>
				<</if>>
			<<else>>
				<<ind>><span class="purple">You need to be <i>holding</i> a lit torch to take the shortcut to the forest.</span>
			<</if>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Disposal Torch Friend
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

<<if $willpowerSuccess and $phase is 1>>
	If you don't look, it isn't real. Belief is power. You repeat this to yourself multiple times. <span class="red">You feel another breath.</span> Don't look. To see is to make real. Belief is power.
	<br><br>

	<span class="green">You shut your eyes, your <<if $worn.upper.name is "chain tunic">>gauntlets<<else>>hands<</if>> gripping the stone wall behind you. After some time, the breathing finally stops.</span>
	<br><br>

	You open your eyes and look up. There was never anything there.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Disposal]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	If you don't look, it isn't real. You try to tell yourself that, over and over. Its breath creeps down your ears, your neck, your spine. <span class="red">You can't help it. You look up.</span>
	<br><br>

	Something in the shape of a person clings to the wall, its head nearly touching yours. It's entirely reflective, yet the light of the torch almost looks to be getting sucked into it. Glossy yellow eyes glare at you.
	<br><br>

	You're frozen. Slowly, cracks form along its head, forming a wide smile.
	<br><br>

	<<set _torchHeld to hcItemLitTorch()>>
	<<set _torchInSconce to $hcItems.find(torch => torch.type is "torch" and torch.state is "lit" and torch.location is "disposal" and torch.inSconce is true)>>
	<<if _torchHeld and _torchInSconce>>
		It slowly brings an elongated hand down to your torch, and its other hand to the torch sconce. At once, it clasps its hands over them both, plunging you into darkness as they fizzle out.
	<<elseif _torchInSconce>>
		It slowly brings an elongated hand over the torch sconce. Its eyes remain locked on you as its smile continues to widen. It closes its hand over the lit torch, plunging you into darkness as it fizzles out.
	<<else>>
		It slowly brings an elongated hand over your torch. Its eyes remain locked on you as its smile continues to widen. It closes its hand over the lit torch, plunging you into darkness as it fizzles out.
	<</if>>
	<<gggstress>><<gggtrauma>><<stress 50>><<trauma 100>>
	<br><br>

	<<run $hcItems.filter(torch => torch.type is "torch" and torch.state is "lit" and ["held", "disposal"].includes(torch.location)).forEach(torch => {torch.state = "snuffed"})>>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Disposal]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Disposal Glassfingers
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $hc.disposals += 10>>
<<if $hc.shortcutCount isnot undefined>><<set $hc.shortcutCount++>><</if>>
<<unset $itemAction>><<unset $itemActionObject>>

You toss your still-burning torch into the channel.
<br><br>

It stops. Mid-air. Just above the water.
<br><br>

A long, glowing yellow appendage hangs from the ceiling, wrapped around the haft of the torch. It slowly retracts, pulling the torch up.
<br><br>

Something shimmers up above. The light of the torch reflects off of it, yet whatever it is seems to be devouring the light itself.
<br><br>

You see four long, glassy fingers wrap around the torch from the yawning blackness. They glow a resplendent mix of colour for a brief moment, before appearing to fill with smoke as the torch rapidly dims.
<br><br>

The torch, fingers, and appendage all wink out of existence at once. You rub your eyes. <<trauma 50>><<gggtrauma>>
<br><br>

<<if $hc.trueEndAvailable>>
	<span class="narration">
		The story of this entity was used to scare younger initiates into obedience. Many of them believed it.
		<br><br>

		It was a creature of glass. Different retellings disagree on whether it was translucent or reflective. Sometimes it was both.
		It was blamed for torches going out prematurely, or pyres failing to burn through the night.
		<<if $hcChallenge.forestNoShortcut>>
			Flockmembers losing their way in the channel was also blamed on this creature.
		<</if>>
		I believe sightings were a product of torch flames exhausting the oxygen in the enclosed space of the channel.
		<br><br>

		<<if $hc.disposals lt 30>>
			The gaoler had its attention. Now it needed to be fed. It favoured objects that were 'tainted.'
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
	</span>
<</if>>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Disposal]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Lizard
<<set _thermoDisable to true>>
<<if $molestationstart is 1>>
	<<set $molestationstart to 0>>
	<<controlloss>>
	<<violence 1>>
	<<neutral 1>>
	<<molested>>
	<<beastCombatInit>>
<</if>>
<<effects>>
<<effectsman>>
<br>
<<beast $enemyno>>
<br><br>

<<stateman>>
<br><br>
<<actionsman>>

<<if _combatend>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Lizard Finish]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Lizard]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Lizard Finish
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

<<if $enemypleasure gte $enemypleasuremax>>
	<<beastejaculation>>

	The <<beasttype>> hisses <<bhis>> satisfaction, and dives back into the watery labyrinth.
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you gather yourself. After more blind stumbling, you find your way back to the dungeon.
	<br><br>

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>
	<<canvas-model-override "mouth" "neutral">>

	<<prisonicon "cell">><<link [[Dungeon (0:20)|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon]]>><<pass 20>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<if $finish is 1>><<encounterEndViolence>><</if>>
	The <<beasttype>> hisses and dives back into the watery labyrinth.
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you gather yourself. After more blind stumbling, you find your way back to the dungeon.

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>
	<<canvas-model-override "mouth" "neutral">>

	<<prisonicon "cell">><<link [[Dungeon (0:20)|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon]]>><<pass 20>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

/* Cloister */
:: Hopeless Cycle Cloister
<<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $bus to "cloister">>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

You are in the temple cloister.
<<if Time.hour gte 7 and Time.hour lte 9 and !$hc.daily.sermon>>
	<span class="blue">The Bishop's Hand is here, preparing for the daily sermon.</span> Your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> sit in lines.
<<elseif Time.dayState is "night">>
	It's eerily quiet.
	<<if (Time.hour gte 23 or Time.hour lte 5)>>
		The stairs to the dungeon have been locked up for the night, and no one prowls the corridors.
	<<else>>
		No one prowls the corridors, but there's still someone standing guard at the stairs to the dungeon.
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	Your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> prowl around the outskirts, emerging from and disappearing into the many passages leading away.
<</if>>
<br><br>

A statue of a six-armed, six-winged angel stands resolute in the centre. The angel appears to be heavy with child.
<br><br>

<<if _hcEvent is "blood">>
	A heavy hand rests on your shoulder. The Bishop's Hand looms before you. "<span class="red">It's time, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>.</span> Bring the witch up at once."
	<br><br>

	You enter the dungeon. There's no one to sanctify you on the way in. You suppose it's pointless since you'll be bringing <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> out anyways.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Enter <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell|Hopeless Cycle Blood Cell]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $stress gte $stressmax>>
	<<hopelessCyclePassout>>
<<elseif $hc.suspicion gte 100>>
	<span class="red">Everything goes dark as a sack is pulled over your head.</span> You're quickly struck in the gut, doubling you over. You're forced to your knees.
	<br><br>

	The last thing you feel is an impact against your head.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Ending E]]>><<pass 4 hours>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $exposed gte 2>>
	You creep around the cloister, concealing your nudity behind a column of gargoyles whenever you hear the shuffle of feet. <<hcSuspicion 2>><<hopelessCycleSus 1>>
	<br><br>

	<b><u>Locations:</u></b><br>
	<<templeicon "quarters">><<link [[Passage to quarters (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Quarters]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<templeicon "garden">><<link [[Passage to garden (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Garden]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<templeicon>><<link [[Main hall (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Temple]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif !$hc.suspicionRevealed and ($hc.suspicion gte 40 or ($hc.suspicion gte 25 and (Time.hour gte 23 or Time.hour lte 4)))>>
	<<set $hc.suspicionRevealed to true>>

	"<<worldMale 'Brother' 'Sister'>> Fayne." <span class="red">A stern, rumbling voice makes you freeze in place.</span> Heavy, familiar footsteps approach.
	<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
		"Up so late. Sneaking around?"
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	You slowly turn to the source.
	<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
		<<if hcItemLitTorch()>>
			An ugly, brown-bearded face is illuminated by your torch.
		<<else>>
			Dim torchlight envelops you.
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	A massive hand comes to rest on your shoulder as the Bishop's Hand towers over you.
	<br><br>

	"We worry for you. Your behaviour as of late has been..." <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> grins.
	"Unusual. Some confessors suspect that the witch has <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> fingers around your soul. I told them to have faith, but our... tolerance... only goes so far."
	<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> chuckles. "Do not fail us, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>. Your family. Think about how they would feel if you had to be locked away with <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>. Purified with <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>."
	<br><br>

	<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> pats you on the shoulder once more before walking off. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> wipes <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> hand on <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> tunic, as if touching you made <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> filthy.
	<br><br>

	<span class="narration">The Bishop's Hand and <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> confessors had been watching the gaoler. Now that <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> knew this, <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> would be more aware of what actions would make them suspicious.</span>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Cloister]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<if Time.hour gte 7 and Time.hour lte 9 and !$hc.daily.sermon>>
		<<templeicon "altar">><<link [[Attend sermon (0:30)|Hopeless Cycle Cloister Sermon]]>><<pass 30>><<trauma -6>><<purity 4>><<hcSuspicion -5 "sermon">><<set $hc.daily.sermon to true>><</link>><<ltrauma>><<gpurity>><<if !$hcChallenge.suspicionSermon>><<hopelessCycleSus -2>><</if>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<if $temple_confessor_intro>>
		<<templeicon "statue">><<link [[Statue of Virgo|Hopeless Cycle Cloister Statue]]>><<set $hcAction to "approach">><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<templeicon "statue">><<link [[Six-armed statue|Hopeless Cycle Cloister Statue]]>><<set $hcAction to "approach">><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<br>
	<div id="hcItems" class="no-numberify"><<hopelessCycleItemLinks>></div>
	<b><u>Locations:</u></b><br>
	<<if Time.dayState is "night" and (Time.hour gte 23 or Time.hour lte 5)>>
		<<if $worn.upper.name is "chain tunic" or hcItemLitTorch()>>
			<<if $worn.upper.name is "chain tunic">>
				<span class="red">Your armour makes you conspicuous.</span>
			<</if>>
			<<if hcItemLitTorch()>>
				<span class="red">Your lit torch will make sneaking impossible.</span>
			<</if>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<prisonicon "cell">><<link [[Sneak into the dungeon (0:02)|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon Sneak]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		A priest stands guard at the top of the dungeon stairs.
		<br>
		<<prisonicon "cell">><<link [[Dungeon <<hcTimeDungeonDisplay>>|Hopeless Cycle Dungeon Enter]]>><</link>>
	<</if>>
	<br>
	<<kitchenicon "soup">><<link [[Dining hall (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Cloister Dining]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>

	<<templeicon $temple_weapon>><<link [[Training room (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Cloister Training]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br><br>

	<<templeicon "quarters">><<link [[Passage to quarters (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Quarters]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<templeicon "garden">><<link [[Passage to garden (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Garden]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<templeicon>><<link [[Main hall (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Temple]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Cloister Training
<<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $bus to "training">>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

<<if Time.dayState isnot "night">>
	You enter one of the training rooms, and find your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> sparring. A weapon rack sits at the back of the room, sporting vicious-looking whips and batons.
<<else>>
	You enter one of the training rooms. It's empty. Despite the heavy use it sees during the day, not a grain of sand lies outside the arena in the centre. A weapon rack sits at the back of the room, sporting vicious-looking whips and batons.
	<br><br>
	You could spar here, during the day.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if _hcEvent is "blood">>
	A heavy hand rests on your shoulder. The Hand looms before you. "<span class="red">It's time, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>.</span> Bring the witch up at once."
	<br><br>

	You enter the dungeon. There's no one to sanctify you on the way in. You suppose it's pointless since you'll be bringing <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> out anyways.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Enter <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell|Hopeless Cycle Blood Cell]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<if Time.dayState isnot "night">>
		<<if $temple_weapon is "baton">>
			<<templeicon "baton">><<link [[Spar <<hcTimeTaskDisplay>>|Hopeless Cycle Spar]]>><<prof baton 4>><<set $temple_spar to 1>><<physique 6>><<tiredness 6>><<hcTimeTaskPass>><<hcSuspicion -1>><<sadism 5>><</link>><<gtiredness>><<gbaton>><<gphysique>><<hopelessCycleSus -1>>
		<<elseif $temple_weapon is "whip">>
			<<templeicon "whip">><<link [[Spar <<hcTimeTaskDisplay>>|Hopeless Cycle Spar]]>><<prof whip 4>><<set $temple_spar to 1>><<physique 6>><<tiredness 6>><<hcTimeTaskPass>><<hcSuspicion -1>><<sadism 5>><</link>><<gtiredness>><<gwhip>><<gphysique>><<hopelessCycleSus -1>>
		<</if>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<bathroomicon "soap">><<link [[Wash yourself (0:10)|Hopeless Cycle Cloister Training]]>><<stress -2>><<wash>><<pass 10>><</link>><<lstress>>
	<br><br>

	<<set _itemsHere.push("bandages")>>
	<div id="hcItems" class="no-numberify"><<hopelessCycleItemLinks>></div>
	<b><u>Locations:</u></b><br>
	<<templeicon "cloister">><<link [[Cloister (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Cloister]]>><<pass 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>


:: Hopeless Cycle Spar
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>><<wearProp "whip" "khaki">>

<<generateTemple 1>><<person1>>

One of your <<sister_npc>>s bows to you. A few of your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> watch from the sidelines.

<<if $rng gte 51>>
	<<set _npcWeapon to "baton">>
	<<He>> wields a baton.
<<else>>
	<<set _npcWeapon to "whip">>
	<<He>> wields a whip.
<</if>>
<br><br>


<<if $prof.whip gte 1000>>
	No one in the order, not even the high priest, can compare to you when it comes to the art of the whip. The battle isn't even close.
	<br><br>

	<<if _npcWeapon is "whip">>
		You expertly dodge every single strike. You know the movements well, after all. Every tiny movement is obvious to you.
		<br><br>

		You let <<him>> tire <<himself>> out, and end the fight with a masterful trip. It was your only attack, because one was all you needed.
	<<else>>
		You make the first strike, landing a precise hit right on <<his>> hand. You follow it up with another, disarming <<him>>. Finally, you wrap your whip around <<his>> leg and trip <<him>>. <<He>> never even got to make a single attack.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	Your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> applaud.
<<else>>
	You're hard to beat with your favoured weapon.
	<<if _npcWeapon is "whip">>
		<<He>> puts up a good fight, but you're far superior. You take a few hits, but end the battle with a decisive strike followed by a trip.
	<<else>>
		You take one good hit, but the rest of the fight goes your way. You manage to get your whip around <<his>> baton, and send it flying off across the room.
	<</if>>
	<<pain 2>><<gpain>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Cloister Training]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Cloister Dining
<<set $location to "old_temple">><<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $bus to "dining">>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
You are in the cloister's dining hall.
<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
	It's deserted.
<<elseif Time.dayState is "dawn">>
	It's quite lively. Many of your siblings are preparing for a long day.
<<else>>
	Some of your siblings sit at long tables.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if _hcEvent is "blood">>
	A heavy hand rests on your shoulder. The Bishop's Hand looms before you. "<span class="red">It's time, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>.</span> Bring the witch up at once."
	<br><br>

	You enter the dungeon. There's no one to sanctify you on the way in. You suppose it's pointless since you'll be bringing <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> out anyways.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Enter <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell|Hopeless Cycle Blood Cell]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $stress gte $stressmax>>
	<<hopelessCyclePassout>>
<<elseif $hc.suspicion gte 100>>
	<span class="red">Everything goes dark as a sack is pulled over your head.</span> You're quickly struck in the gut, doubling you over. You're forced to your knees.
	<br><br>

	The last thing you feel is an impact against your head.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Ending E]]>><<pass 4 hours>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
		<span class="red">The food is locked away for the night.</span>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<if !$hc.daily.foodPlayer>>
			<<foodicon "eat">><<link [[Eat <<hcTimeTaskDisplay 30>>|Hopeless Cycle Cloister Dining Eat]]>><<hcTimeTaskPass 30>><<set $hc.daily.foodPlayer to true>><<tiredness -6>><<stress -24>><<trauma -12>><</link>><<lltiredness>><<llstress>><<ltrauma>>
			<br>
			<<if hcItemHasFreeHand()>>
				<<foodstufficon "salmon_wellington">><<link [[Leave with your portion|Hopeless Cycle Cloister Dining]]>><<run hcItemAdd({ type: "food", name: "stolen food", location: "held", origin: "dining", dirtyOnDrop: V.hcChallenge.itemDirty })>><<set $hc.daily.foodPlayer to true>><<hcSuspicion 5>><</link>><<hopelessCycleSus 1>>
				<br>
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
		<<if !$hc.daily.foodWitch and hcItemHasFreeHand()>>
			<<hcicon "food">><<link [[`Take a portion for $prisoner.name`|Hopeless Cycle Cloister Dining]]>><<run hcItemAdd({ type: "food", name: "prison gruel", location: "held", origin: "dining", dirtyOnDrop: V.hcChallenge.itemDirty })>><<set $hc.daily.foodWitch to true>><</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<if !hcItemHasFreeHand() and (!$hc.daily.foodPlayer or !$hc.daily.foodWitch)>>
			<span class="red">You need a free hand to pick up food.</span>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<br>

	<div id="hcItems" class="no-numberify"><<hopelessCycleItemLinks>></div>
	<b><u>Locations:</u></b><br>
	<<templeicon "cloister">><<link [[Cloister (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Cloister]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Cloister Dining Eat
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>><<wearProp "spoon">>

You sit with your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> to eat your meal. It's hearty and flavourful.
<br><br>

<<if $hc.nightBreakIn is "tonight">>
	<<set $hc.nightBreakIn to "heard">>
	You overhear some of your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> talking.
	<br><br>

	"...gets the witch all to <<worldMale 'himself' 'herself'>>. Aye. <span class="red">Tonight, I think I'll sneak down there and...</span>" You lose the rest in the noise of the hall.
<<else>>
	<<set $hc.chatter ||= []>>
	You overhear some of your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> talking.
	<br><br>

	<<cleareventpool>>
	<<if !$hc.chatter.includes("hc_bucket_hint")>>
		<<addinlineevent "hc_bucket_hint">>
			<<set $hc.chatter.pushUnique("hc_bucket_hint")>>
			"Where are all the damned buckets?"
			<br>
			"Everyone always needs one. No one puts them back where they belong."
			<br>
			"Can we make the initiates round them all up?"
			<br>
			"Don't bother. They'll be missing again within the hour. I swear, I saw one of them grow limbs and crawl into the forest."
			<br>
			"You fucked in the head? Do I need to call the confessors?"
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>
	<<if !$hc.chatter.includes("hc_bed_hint")>>
		<<addinlineevent "hc_bed_hint">>
			<<set $hc.chatter.pushUnique("hc_bed_hint")>>
			"The night watch isn't allowed to search under occupied bunks."
			<br>
			"You know this how?"
			<br>
			"I've been smuggling surplus alcohol under mine for months, and no one has said a thing."
			<br>
			"Thanks for the free blackmail material."
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>
	<<if !$hc.chatter.includes("hc_disposal_hint")>>
		<<addinlineevent "hc_disposal_hint" 2>>
			<<set $hc.chatter.pushUnique("hc_disposal_hint")>>
			"I'm glad I'll never have to walk the disposal channel again. I could never stand the... <i>things</i> down there."
			<br>
			"You whine like a babe. Afraid Gran Glassfingers will find you? You need a nursery rhyme?"
			<br>
			"Don't joke about that. It's a monstrosity like any other. This one's just kept docile by all the tainted refuse we toss."
			<br>
			"You only give it power by believing it's real."
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>
	<<if $hc.chatter.includes("hc_disposal_hint") and !$hc.chatter.includes("hc_disposal_hint2")>>
		<<addinlineevent "hc_disposal_hint2" 2>>
			<<set $hc.chatter.pushUnique("hc_disposal_hint2")>>
			"Have you ever been down in the disposal channel yourself?"
			<br>
			"Nay."
			<br>
			"Be glad. Always feels like you're being watched down there. It's something about the dark, and the sound of the rushing water. Found myself staring often, feeling the strange urge to toss my torch into the waterway."
			<br>
			"Maybe you just have a guardian angel watching you."
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>
	<<if $hc.chatter.includes("hc_disposal_hint2") and !$hc.chatter.includes("hc_disposal_hint3")>>
		<<addinlineevent "hc_disposal_hint3">>
			<<set $hc.chatter.pushUnique("hc_disposal_hint3")>>
			"Have you ever gone to the disposal channel and just... snuffed all the torches? Let yourself be bathed in the darkness?"
			<br>
			"Yes. Once. Never again."
			<br>
			"Coward. I've peered into the darkness twice and nothing's happened. It's a nice place to gather my thoughts."
			<br>
			"I don't even need to report you to the priests, you'll end up stumbling into your own punishment. Third time's the charm."
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>
	<<if !$hc.chatter.includes("hc_lake_hint")>>
		<<addinlineevent "hc_lake_hint">>
			<<set $hc.chatter.pushUnique("hc_lake_hint")>>
			"Do you ever wonder if there's someone buried in the disposal channel?"
			<br>
			"Not until just now."
			<br>
			"I've been having dreams. There are bones down there, waiting to be reunited with something. Something from the source of the water."
			<br>
			"You've been taking too many confessions. You're spouting nonsense."
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>
	<<if !$hc.chatter.includes("hc_chatter_1")>>
		<<addinlineevent "hc_chatter_1">>
			<<set $hc.chatter.pushUnique("hc_chatter_1")>>
			"Burn anything interesting lately?"
			<br>
			"Aye, found some wooden busts when we captured the witch. Each one had a hat. Burned those too. One of them got away, though."
			<br>
			"What? The fuck do you mean, 'one got away?' Did it grow limbs and crawl?"
			<br>
			You don't hear an answer.
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>
	<<if !$hc.chatter.includes("hc_chatter_2")>>
		<<addinlineevent "hc_chatter_2">>
			<<set $hc.chatter.pushUnique("hc_chatter_2")>>
			"There are so few monstrosities around now. It almost feels as though we're not needed."
			<br>
			"Stay vigilant. They're just waiting for us to let our guard down."
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>
	<<if !$hc.chatter.includes("hc_chatter_3")>>
		<<addinlineevent "hc_chatter_3">>
			<<set $hc.chatter.pushUnique("hc_chatter_3")>>
			"Have you seen the new high priest around?"
			<br>
			"No one has seen <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> much. The Bishop's Hand has taken most of <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> duties."
			<br>
			"<<worldMale 'King' 'Queen'>> shit-beard's trying to make <<worldMale 'himself' 'herself'>> more important than <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> is."
			<br>
			"Shut your mouth before I tell <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> you said that."
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>
	<<if !$hc.chatter.includes("hc_chatter_4")>>
		<<addinlineevent "hc_chatter_4">>
			<<set $hc.chatter.pushUnique("hc_chatter_4")>>
			"I can't stop staring at the idol of Virgo."
			<br>
			"It's a masterwork, is it not?"
			<br>
			"It's confusing. It seems intentionally provocative. Why did they have to put so much detail in the parts we're not supposed to look at?"
			<br>
			"You should visit the confessional."
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>
	<<addinlineevent "hc_chatter_misc">>
		<<set _lines1 to [
			"I wish our armour was more revealing.",
			"The fruits speak to me. They beg to be devoured.",
			"I find myself wondering if our batons would make for a good purging aid.",
			"I adore watching the initiates undergo the Trial of Purity. Their feet, covered in soot...",
			"There's an angel in our ranks. My last purge was truly divine. I must learn their identity, and invoke the Rite of Promise."
		]>>
		<<set _lines2 to [
			"Please repent.",
			"I'm telling the priests.",
			"I am not a confessor, I do not need to hear that.",
			"This is not your true heart. Seek contrition."
		]>>
		"<<print _lines1.pluck()>>"
		<br>
		"<<print _lines2.pluck()>>"
		<br>
		They're just chattering. Nothing useful.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<runeventpool>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Cloister Dining]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Cloister Sermon
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

<<generateTemple 1>><<person1>>
You join your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> on the floor.
<br><br>

A <<priest>> leads you all in prayer. You keep your head bowed.
<br><br>

When the prayers are finished, the Bishop's Hand steps forward and clears <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> throat.
<<if $hc.daysPassed is 1>>
	"As many of you already know, we have at last captured and imprisoned the witch that was working <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> vile magic on the town."
	<br><br>

	You hear murmurs from the gathered flock.
	<br><br>

	"<<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> belongings have been burned. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> will rot in the dungeon until the red moon, when <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> will face redemption."
	Your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> cheer.
	<br><br>

	"All who enter or leave the dungeon are to be sanctified before and after, to prevent contamination. All faithful within the dungeon are to leave before nightfall."
<<elseif $hc.daysPassed is 2>>
	"The laymen have begun to make their displeasure at our capture of the witch known. The night watch will be moved from interior to exterior patrols for the foreseeable future."
<<elseif $hc.daysPassed is 5 and !$hcChallenge.dogsEarly>>
	"Representatives from House dogbotherer- apologies, House Romilly, will be taking residence with us for a number of days." Some members of the flock laugh.
	<br><br>

	"They wish to sell us some of their trained hounds. <span class="blue">They will operate on the temple grounds each day until dusk.</span> Get used to the noise."
<<elseif $hc.daysPassed is 6 and !$hcChallenge.waterEarly>>
	<<set $hc.wellTainted to true>>
	"The well is to be left unused until after the red moon. <span class="red">Its water has turned foul.</span>" Murmurs from the flock follow.
	<br><br>

	"No cause for alarm. <span class="blue">Our clean water must be sourced from the lake until then.</span>"
<<elseif Time.lastDayOfMonth is $hc.day>>
	"All members of the flock are to prepare for tonight's ritual. The witch's gaoler will bring <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> to the altar come nightfall."
	<br><br>

	The flock grows noisy with murmurs.
	<br><br>

	"Virgo is with us. Have faith."
<<else>>
	<<cleareventpool>>

	<<addinlineevent "hc_sermon_1">>
		"All <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> are to remember that the statue of Virgo is not to be molested. It is a trial of your faith like any other."
	<</addinlineevent>>
	<<addinlineevent "hc_sermon_2">>
		"Rumours that House O'Cuinn has consorted with the Elkseed Cult are to be quashed at once. This is a sensitive matter."
	<</addinlineevent>>
	<<addinlineevent "hc_sermon_3">>
		"All members of the flock are forbidden from taking leisure time at the lake, effective immediately."
	<</addinlineevent>>
	<<addinlineevent "hc_sermon_4">>
		"For the last time, there is no beast in the disposal channel. Are you all children?"
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<runeventpool>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

With the announcement finished, the flock disperses. Some head to the dining hall, while others walk to the training rooms or the garden.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Cloister]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Cloister Statue
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<set $temple_burden to Math.clamp($temple_burden, 0, 50)>>
<<if $hcAction is "approach">>
	<<if $temple_confessor_intro>>
		You approach the statue of Virgo.
	<<else>>
		You approach the statue.
	<</if>>
	It appears to be made of marble. Its belly is discoloured from your siblings rubbing it for good luck.
	Its wings are spread out wide, and its middle arms are open as if to welcome someone in a loving embrace.
	<br><br>

	You feel as though this gesture is aimed at all of your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>>. A rapturous thanks for a great sacrifice made. <span class="green">The arrow of time has skipped midnight, for now.</span>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<unset $hcAction>>

<<if !$hcChallenge.faithBurden>>
	<<if $temple_burden lt 50>>
		<<templeicon "statue">><<link [[Embrace (0:05)|Hopeless Cycle Cloister Statue]]>><<pass 5>><<set $itemAction to "embrace">><<set $temple_burden += 5>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<if $temple_burden gte 1>>
		<<templeicon "statue">><<link [[Surrender (0:05)|Hopeless Cycle Cloister Statue]]>><<pass 5>><<set $itemAction to "surrender">><<set $temple_burden -= 5>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<</if>>

<<templeicon "cloister">><<link [[Leave|Hopeless Cycle Cloister]]>><</link>>
<br>


/* Main Hall */
:: Hopeless Cycle Temple
<<set $location to "old_temple">><<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $bus to "temple">>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<switch $hcAction>>
	<<case "pray">>You spend an hour praying to restore your faith.
	<<case "mass">>You attend mass amidst your fellow worshippers. The Bishop's melodic voice lulls you into a sense of belonging. Your faith in the order is greatly restored.
	<<default>>You are in the main hall of the temple. Stone walls and pillars tower into darkness. Rows of seats face an altar at the end of the room.
<</switch>>
<<unset $hcAction>>
<br><br>

<<if _hcEvent is "blood">>
	A heavy hand rests on your shoulder. The Bishop's Hand looms before you. "<span class="red">It's time, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>.</span> Bring the witch up at once."
	<br><br>

	You enter the dungeon. There's no one to sanctify you on the way in. You suppose it's pointless since you'll be bringing <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> out anyways.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Enter <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell|Hopeless Cycle Blood Cell]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $stress gte $stressmax>>
	<<hopelessCyclePassout>>
<<elseif $hc.suspicion gte 100>>
	<span class="red">Everything goes dark as a sack is pulled over your head.</span> You're quickly struck in the gut, doubling you over. You're forced to your knees.
	<br><br>

	The last thing you feel is an impact against your head.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Ending E]]>><<pass 4 hours>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $exposed gte 2>>
	You hide behind one of the pillars to conceal your <<nudity>>. <<hcSuspicion 2>><<hopelessCycleSus 1>>
	<br><br>

	<b><u>Locations:</u></b><br>
	<<templeicon "cloister">><<link [[Cloister (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Cloister]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br><br>

	<<templeicon "garden">><<link [[Garden (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Garden]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<templeicon "quarters">><<link [[Barracks (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Quarters]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $hc.daysPassed gte 4 and Time.dayState is "day" and !$hc.bailiff>>
	<<set $hc.bailiff to true>>
	<<generate1>><<person1>>
	You hear the Bishop's Hand talking to someone. You round the corner, and see a <<personsimple>> in a suit of armour accompanied by three bodyguards.
	<br><br>

	You recognise <<his>> coat of arms. A serpent winding around a scale. House Bailiff. You listen in.
	<br><br>

	"...into our custody immediately." <<He>> points at the Hand, speaking with authority. "You had no grounds to seize our property."
	<br><br>

	"There's no one here by that name," the Hand interrupts with a grin. "If you're searching for an angel, you're welcome to join us in prayer."
	<br><br>

	The <<personsimple>> scowls. "You are no different to the cults you claim to punish. We are prepared to take up arms."
	<br><br>

	The Hand lets out a belly laugh. "You're welcome to try." <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> leans in, prompting each bodyguard to draw a sword. "We have plenty of empty cells and eager whips."
	<br><br>

	The <<personsimple>> takes a step back. "Barbarians." <<He>> turns to leave. "We will be back."
	<br><br>

	"You won't," the Hand says under <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> breath.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Temple]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<if Time.weekDay is 1 and Time.hour gte 10 and Time.hour lte 12 and $hc.daily.massAttended isnot 1 and $exposed lte 0>>
		<<templeicon "altar">><<link [[Attend mass (1:00)|Hopeless Cycle Temple]]>><<set $hcAction to "mass">><<pass 60>><<set $hc.daily.massAttended to 1>><<stress -100>><<trauma -50>><</link>><<lllstress>><<llltrauma>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<templeicon "pray">><<link [[Pray (1:00)|Hopeless Cycle Temple]]>><<set $hcAction to "pray">><<pass 60>><<stress -2>><<trauma -6>><</link>><<lstress>><<ltrauma>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<br>

	<div id="hcItems" class="no-numberify"><<hopelessCycleItemLinks>></div>
	<b><u>Locations:</u></b><br>
	<<templeicon "cloister">><<link [[Cloister (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Cloister]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br><br>

	<<templeicon "garden">><<link [[Garden (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Garden]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<templeicon "quarters">><<link [[Barracks (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Quarters]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<templeicon "prayer room">><<link [[Prayer room (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Prayer Room]]>><<set $hcAction to "enter">><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>


/* Garden */
:: Hopeless Cycle Garden
<<set $location to "old_temple">><<set $outside to 1>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $bus to "garden">>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

You are in the temple garden. Rows of flowers lead away from the temple proper, becoming more unruly as they approach the forest. It's unclear where the temple grounds end and forest begins.

<<if Time.dayState is "dawn">>
	Sunlight bleeds through the branches of trees. Your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> tend to a bed of hot coals.
	<<if $hc.dogs>>
		A small dog kennel has been set up. The dogs are waking up for the day.
	<</if>>
<<elseif Time.dayState is "day">>
	The sun gleams above a curtain of trees. Your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> tend to a bed of hot coals.
	<<if $hc.dogs>>
		A small dog kennel has been set up, and representatives from House Romilly show off their trained hounds.
	<</if>>
<<elseif Time.dayState is "dusk">>
	The trees sway in the wind. Your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> prepare for this evening's pyre.
	<<if $hc.dogs>>
		A small dog kennel has been set up. The dogs have gone quiet.
	<</if>>
<<elseif Time.dayState is "night">>
	It's nearly pitch-black.
	<<if Time.hour gte 20 or Time.hour lte 2>>
		A large pyre burns further away.
	<<else>>
		The remains of the nightly pyre smoulder nearby.
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if Time.dayState isnot "night" or hcItemLitTorch()>>
	<br>
	<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
		<span class="orange">Your torch lights up the night.</span>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	There's a well here.
	<<set _canSee to true>>
<<else>>
	<br>
	<span class="red">It's too dark to see anything near the well, or to work in the garden.</span>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if _hcEvent is "blood">>
	A heavy hand rests on your shoulder. The Bishop's Hand looms before you. "<span class="red">It's time, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>.</span> Bring the witch here at once."
	<br><br>

	You enter the dungeon. There's no one to sanctify you on the way in. You suppose it's pointless since you'll be bringing <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> out anyways.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Enter <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell|Hopeless Cycle Blood Cell]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $stress gte $stressmax>>
	<<hopelessCyclePassout>>
<<elseif $hc.suspicion gte 100>>
	<span class="red">Everything goes dark as a sack is pulled over your head.</span> You're quickly struck in the gut, doubling you over. You're forced to your knees.
	<br><br>

	The last thing you feel is an impact against your head.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Ending E]]>><<pass 4 hours>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $exposed gte 2>>
	You hide behind a hedge to conceal your <<nudity>>. <<hcSuspicion 2>><<hopelessCycleSus 1>>
	<br><br>

	<b><u>Locations:</u></b><br>
	<<wolficon>><<link [[Temple main hall (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Temple]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<templeicon "cloister">><<link [[Passage to cloister (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Cloister]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<foresticon>><<link [[Forest (0:10)|Hopeless Cycle Forest]]>><<set $hcForest to 0>><<pass 10>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $hc.daysPassed gte 6 and !$hc.wellTainted and _canSee>>
	<<set $hc.wellTainted to true>>
	<<generateTemple 1>><<person1>>
	One of your <<sister_npc>>s stands by the well, looking perplexed. <<He>> waves as you approach.
	<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
		<<He>> holds a torch of <<his>> own. "Hail, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>. It seems we're both troubled tonight."
	<<else>>
		"Hail, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>. We face troubles."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<He>> nods down to a bucket full of water. <span class="red">Hues of red and purple are mixed into it.</span>
	"Our well's water has gone foul. An ill omen."
	<br><br>

	<<He>> shakes <<his>> head. "All will be right again once the red moon passes. Until then, <span class="blue">we must get our water from the lake.</span>"
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Garden]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<if _canSee>>
		<<set _itemsHere.push("water")>>
		<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("brand")>>
			<<set _itemsHere.push("herbs")>>
		<</if>>
		<<templeicon "garden">><<link [[Work in the garden <<hcTimeTaskDisplay>>|Hopeless Cycle Garden Work]]>><<hcTimeTaskPass>><<stress -6>><<hcSuspicion -1>><<tiredness 6>><<tending 1>><</link>><<lstress>><<gtending>><<hopelessCycleSus -1>><<gtiredness>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<if $hc.dogs and Time.dayState is "day">>
		<br>
		The hounds are out and about.
		<<if $hc.dogs.includes("loud")>>
			<<if $hc.dogs.count("loud") gt 1>>
				<span class="pink"><<number $hc.dogs.count("loud")>> of them are barking particularly loudly, seeming neglected by their masters.</span>
				Some food from the dining hall might keep one of them quiet, or you could find something to play with it.
			<<else>>
				<span class="pink">One of them is barking particularly loudly, seeming neglected by its masters.</span>
				Some food from the dining hall might keep it quiet, or you could find something to play with it.
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<span class="green">The loudest of the hounds <<= $hcChallenge.dogsDouble ? "have" : "has">> been quieted.</span>
		<</if>>
		<br>
		<<set _stick to hcItemCanReach("torch", t => t.state isnot "lit")>>
		<<set _food to hcItemsOnScreen(f => f.type is "food" and !f.name isnot "stolen fruit" and !f.used and !f.dirty)>>
		<<for _i to 0; _i lt $hc.dogs.length; _i++>>
			<<capture _i, _food, _f>>
				<<if $hc.dogs[_i] is "loud">>
					<<if _stick>>
						<<animalicon "dog">><<link [[Play tug-of-war with it using a _stick.state torch (0:15)|Hopeless Cycle Garden Dog Play]]>><<set $phase to _i>><<pass 15>><</link>>
						<br>
					<</if>>
					<<if _food>>
						<<for _f range _food>>
							<<hcicon _f>><<link [[`Feed it _f.name (0:05)`|Hopeless Cycle Garden Dog Feed]]>><<set $phase to _i>><<pass 5>><<set $hcDogFood to _f.name>><<run hcItemRemove(_f)>><</link>>
							<br>
						<</for>>
					<</if>>
				<<else>>
					<<animalicon "dog">><<link [[Pet the dog (0:05)|Hopeless Cycle Garden]]>><<set $hc.dogsTimer[_i]++>><<pass 5>><<stress -3>><<set $itemAction to "petTheDog">><</link>><<lstress>>
					<br>
				<</if>>
			<</capture>>
		<</for>>
	<</if>>
	<br>

	<div id="hcItems" class="no-numberify"><<hopelessCycleItemLinks>></div>
	<b><u>Locations:</u></b><br>
	<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
		<<lakeicon "campfire">><<link [[Approach the pyre|Hopeless Cycle Pyre]]>><<set $hcAction to "approach">><</link>>
		<br><br>
	<<else>>
		<<templeicon "trial">><<link [[Approach the bed of coals|Hopeless Cycle Pyre]]>><<set $hcAction to "approach">><</link>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<wolficon>><<link [[Temple main hall (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Temple]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<templeicon "cloister">><<link [[Passage to cloister (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Cloister]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<foresticon>><<link [[Forest (0:10)|Hopeless Cycle Forest]]>><<set $hcForest to 0>><<pass 10>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Garden Dog Play
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<set _stick to hcItemCanReach("torch", t => t.state isnot "lit")>>

You grab your _stick.state torch by the top, and hold out the bottom to the dog. It immediately perks up and grabs it in its mouth.
<br><br>

<<if $rng gte 51>>
	It's a bit stronger than you thought. It manages to take it from your grasp, and runs away from you! You chase it around the temple grounds.
	Its handlers seem very amused. <<physique 2>><<stress -3>><<tiredness 2>><<lstress>><<gtiredness>>
	<br><br>

	You eventually manage to catch up, and play a short game of tug of war.
<<else>>
	Its tail wags as you fight for the torch. Its handlers don't seem to mind the help keeping it occupied.
<</if>>
<br><br>

When you're done, it rolls over. You rub its belly. That should hopefully keep it quiet.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Garden]]>><<set $hc.dogs[$phase] to "quiet">><<set $hc.dogsTimer[$phase] to 5>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Garden Dog Feed
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

You put down the $hcDogFood in front of the dog. It perks up and digs in right away.
<br><br>

<<if $hcDogFood is "prison gruel">>
	It does not seem to mind the quality at all.
<<else>>
	It's probably the best food it will ever eat.
<</if>>
<br><br>

One of the handlers sees you and shoos you away, picking up the <<= $hcDogFood is "prison gruel" ? "bowl" : "plate">>. Hopefully this will keep the dog quiet.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Garden]]>><<set $hc.dogs[$phase] to "quiet">><<set $hc.dogsTimer[$phase] to 5>><<unset $hcDogFood>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Garden Work
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

You spend an hour working in the garden. You lament that there aren't more buckets to use.
<br><br>

<<if _hcEvent is "blood">>
	A heavy hand rests on your shoulder. The Bishop's Hand looms before you. "<span class="red">It's time, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>.</span> Bring the witch up at once."
	<br><br>

	You enter the dungeon. There's no one to sanctify you on the way in. You suppose it's pointless since you'll be bringing <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> out anyways.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Enter <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell|Hopeless Cycle Blood Cell]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $hc.suspicion gte 100>>
	<span class="red">Everything goes dark as a sack is pulled over your head.</span> You're quickly struck in the gut, doubling you over. You're forced to your knees.
	<br><br>

	The last thing you feel is an impact against your head.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Ending E]]>><<pass 4 hours>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $stress gte $stressmax>>
	<<hopelessCyclePassout>>
<<else>>
	<<if Time.dayState isnot "night" or hcItemLitTorch()>>
		<<link [[Keep working <<hcTimeTaskDisplay>>|Hopeless Cycle Garden Work]]>><<hcTimeTaskPass>><<stress -6>><<hcSuspicion -1>><<tiredness 6>><<tending 1>><</link>><<lstress>><<gtending>><<hopelessCycleSus -1>><<gtiredness>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<span class="red">It's too dark to continue working in the garden.</span>
		<br>
	<</if>>

	<<link [[Enough working|Hopeless Cycle Garden]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<set _loc to hcItemHasFreeHand() ? "held" : "garden">>
	<<capture _loc>>
		<<link [[Steal some fruit|Hopeless Cycle Garden]]>><<run hcItemAdd({ type: "food", name: "stolen fruit", location: _loc, origin: "garden", dirty: 0, dirtyOnDrop: true })>><<endevent>><<hcSuspicion 5>><</link>><<hopelessCycleSus 1>>
		<br>
	<</capture>>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Pyre
<<set $location to "old_temple">><<set $outside to 1>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $bus to "pyre">>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
You are in the open temple grounds.
<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
	<<if $hcAction is "approach">>
		You approach the pyre.
		<<if Time.hour gte 20 or Time.hour lte 2>>
			<<worldMale 'Brothers' 'Sisters'>> and <<worldFemale 'sisters' 'brothers'>> in black robes greet you as they commit tainted items to the blaze.
		<<else>>
			The remains are smouldering, but would still be enough to re-ignite a torch.
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<<if Time.hour gte 20 or Time.hour lte 2>>
		<<set _itemsHere.push("fire")>>
	<</if>>
	<<set _canIgnite to true>>
	<<unset $hcAction>>
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	<<if ["dawn","day"].includes(Time.dayState)>>
		<<set _canIgnite to true>>
		Some initiates tend a bed of coals. Occasionally, someone tries to walk across.
		<br><br>

		<<if !$hc.daily.trialOfPurity>>
			<<link [[Attempt the Trial of Purity <<hcTimeTaskDisplay>>|Hopeless Cycle Firewalk]]>><<hcTimeTaskPass>><<set $hc.daily.trialOfPurity to true>><</link>><<gwillpower>><<hopelessCycleSus -1>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		Your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> prepare for this evening's pyre.
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br>

<div id="hcItems" class="no-numberify"><<hopelessCycleItemLinks>></div>
<b><u>Locations:</u></b><br>
<<templeicon "garden">><<link [[Garden|Hopeless Cycle Garden]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Firewalk
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

<<if !$hc.firewalk>>
	<<set $hc.firewalk to 1>><<set $fire to 1>>

	The <<monk>> and initiates watch as the coals heat. They soon glow. The initiates lift their shovels, and push the topmost coals onto the earth. They soon have the fire spread into a thin rectangle, its foot beside yours.
	<br><br>

	<<feetstrip>>

	Smoke rises from the coals. You take a deep breath, and step on them. It's warm.
	<br><br>

	<<templeicon "trialcontinue">><<link [[Continue|Hopeless Cycle Firewalk]]>><<set $hc.firewalk++>><</link>><<gpain>>
	<br>
<<elseif $hc.firewalk gte 6>>
	<<unset $fire>>
	You take the final step. It hurts, but you're across.
	<<pain 6>>
	<br><br>

	The initiates applaud, along with several of your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> standing on a balcony back at the temple, watching over the hedge. You examine your soles. They're covered in soot, but not burnt at all.
	<<hcSuspicion -5>><<hopelessCycleSus -2>>
	<br><br>

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endevent>>
	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Pyre]]>><<run delete $hc.firewalk>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<switch $hc.firewalk>>
		<<case 1>>
			You step forward. You feel the coals heat beneath you.
			<<pain 1>>
		<<case 2>>
			You step forward again. The coals are even hotter.
			<<pain 2>>
		<<case 3>>
			You step forward again, now about halfway across the coals. The heat continues to build.
			<<pain 3>>
		<<case 4>>
			You tense as your foot comes down again, the coals now hotter still.
			<<pain 4>>
		<<case 5>>
			Your foot comes down again. You're so close.
			<<pain 5>>
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>

	<<if (currentSkillValue('willpower') / 10) gte ((100 - Math.floor($purity / 10)) + random(1, 100))>>
		<span class="green">You press on.</span><<gwillpower>><<willpower 1>><<hcSuspicion -1>><<hopelessCycleSus -1>>
		<<set _success to true>>
	<<else>>
		<span class="red">You feel your feet burning. You leap off the coals onto the cool dirt.</span><<ggwillpower>><<willpower 10>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<if _success>>
		<<templeicon "trialcontinue">><<link [[Continue|Hopeless Cycle Firewalk]]>><<set $hc.firewalk++>><</link>><<gpain>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<templeicon "trialbail">><<link [[Jump off|Hopeless Cycle Firewalk Jump]]>><<run delete $hc.firewalk>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Firewalk Jump
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<unset $fire>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

You jump from the fire. The cool earth feels wonderful on your feet.
<br><br>

<<clotheson>>
<<endevent>>
<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Pyre]]>><</link>>
<br>


/* Forest */
:: Hopeless Cycle Forest
<<set $location to "forest">><<set $outside to 1>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $bus to "forest">>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<if $hcForest lte 0>>
	You are on the outskirts of the forest. It used to regularly overgrow into the temple's garden.
<<else>>
	You are in the forest, surrounded by nature.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if $hcForest lte 0>><div id="hcItems" class="no-numberify"><<hopelessCycleItemLinks>></div><</if>>
<b><u>Locations:</u></b><br>

<<if $hcForest gte 25>>
	<<lakeicon>><<link [[Lake (0:10)|Hopeless Cycle Lake]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>

<<if $hcForest lt 25>>
	<<getinicon>><<link [[Travel deeper into the forest (0:10)|Hopeless Cycle Forest]]>><<pass 10>><<hcForest "forward">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $hcForest gt 0>>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Travel towards the temple (0:10)|Hopeless Cycle Forest]]>><<pass 10>><<hcForest "back">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

<<if between($hcForest, 15, 19) and $hc.forestPassage>>
	There's a natural cave that merges with the disposal channel here.
	<<if $hc.forestPassage and $hc.shortcutCount isnot undefined>>
		<br>
		<<if $hc.shortcutCount gt 1>>
			You feel you have permission to take the shortcut to the disposal channel <span class="blue"><<number $hc.shortcutCount>></span> more times.
		<<elseif $hc.shortcutCount is 1>>
			You feel you have permission to take the shortcut to the disposal channel <span class="blue">one</span> more time.
			<span class="pink">You would not be able to return here. It would be a one way trip.</span>
		<<else>>
			You feel you <span class="red">do not have permission</span> to take the shortcut to the disposal channel.
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<<if hcItemLitTorch()>>
		<br>
		<<if $hcChallenge.forestNoShortcut and !$hc.shortcutCount>>
			<<sewericon>><<link [[Passage to disposal channel (0:20)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<<else>>
			<<sewericon>><<link [[Passage to disposal channel (0:20)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut]]>><<pass 20>><<set $hcForest to 0>><</link>>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		<span class="red">You'll need a torch to traverse it.</span>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<<elseif between($hcForest, 15, 19) and !$hc.forestPassage>>
	<<if hcItemLitTorch()>>
		<<set $hc.forestPassage to true>>
		<br>
		By the light of your torch, you spot the opening of a cave.
		<span class="gold">It looks like it leads to the disposal channel.</span>
		<br>
		<<if $hcChallenge.forestNoShortcut and $hc.shortcutCount lt 1>>
			<<sewericon>><<link [[Passage to disposal channel (0:20)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<<else>>
			<<sewericon>><<link [[Passage to disposal channel (0:20)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut]]>><<pass 20>><<set $hcForest to 0>><</link>>
		<</if>>
		<br>
	<<elseif !$hc.forestHint>>
		<<set $hc.forestHint to true>>
		You can make out the shape of something, but it leads into darkness.
		<span class="blue">Maybe if you had a torch, you would be able to tell what it was.</span>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<<elseif $hcForest lte 0>>
	<<templeicon "garden">><<link [[Temple garden (0:10)|Hopeless Cycle Garden]]>><<pass 10>><<set $hcForest to 0>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

/* Lake */
:: Hopeless Cycle Lake
<<set $location to "lake">><<set $outside to 1>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $bus to "lake">>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
You are at the lake. It isn't wise to venture so far alone.
<br><br>

<<set _itemsHere.push("water")>>

<<set _bones to hcItemCanReach("bones")>>
<<if _bones>>
	<<capture _bones>>
		<<hcicon "bones">><<link [[Toss the bones into the lake|Hopeless Cycle Wraith]]>><<run hcItemRemove(_bones)>><</link>>
		<br><br>
	<</capture>>
<</if>>

<<if !$hc.lakeBucket>>
	<span class="gold">There's a bucket here. It looks like it's from the temple.</span>
	<br>
	<<if hcItemHasFreeHand()>>
		<<hcicon "bucket">><<link [[Take it|Hopeless Cycle Lake Bucket]]>><<set $hc.lakeBucket to true>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<</if>>

<div id="hcItems" class="no-numberify"><<hopelessCycleItemLinks>></div>
<b><u>Locations:</u></b><br>

<<lakeicon>><<link [[Forest (0:10)|Hopeless Cycle Forest]]>><<set $hcForest to 25>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Lake Bucket
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

You pick up the bucket.
<<if $settings.tentaclesEnabled>>
	<span class="red">A cluster of slimy limbs erupt from it and wrap around your head!</span> <<stress 24>><<ggstress>>
	<br><br>

	Many eyes glare at you from within.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Lake Bucket Tentacles]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You look inside.
	<br><br>

	A massive eye glares at you from the bottom. <<ggtrauma>><<trauma 24>><<bodyliquid "face" "goo" 2>>
	<br><br>

	You're lying on the grass. Your eyes feel strange. The bucket is over your face. There's nothing inside of it.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Lake]]>><<pass 10>><<run hcItemAdd({ type: "container", name: "bucket", location: "held", origin: "garden", persists: true, containerID: "gardenBucket2", capacity: 3 })>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Lake Bucket Tentacles
<<set _thermoDisable to true>>

<<if $molestationstart is 1>>
	<<set $molestationstart to 0>>
	<<set $combat to 1>>
	<<set $enemytype to "tentacles">>
	<<molested>>
	<<controlloss>>
	<<tentaclestart 5 15>>
<</if>>
<<statetentacles>>

<<effects>>
<<effectstentacles>>
<<tentacles>>
<<actionstentacles>>

<<if $tentacles.active lte ($tentacles.max / 2)>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Lake Bucket Tentacles Finish]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Lake Bucket Tentacles]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Lake Bucket Tentacles Finish
<<effects>>

You grab one of the tentacles, grab the rim of the bucket with your other hand, and pull.
You yank out an undulating mass of... something. A lesser monstrosity. Deprived of its shell, it flees into the forest, writhing and dragging itself along with its tentacles.
<br><br>

<span class="gold">You triumphantly claim your new bucket.</span>
<br><br>

<<clotheson>>
<<endcombat>>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Lake]]>><<run hcItemAdd({ type: "container", name: "bucket", location: "held", origin: "garden", persists: true, containerID: "gardenBucket2", capacity: 3 })>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Wraith
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<if $hc.trueEndAvailable>>
	<span class="narration">
		There are many tales about the lake. A popular one in the Celtic circles is of the 'Bean Sídhe of Loch Bláithín', a fey-like spirit that foretold omens, keened for lost family members, or, in some tales, granted wishes.
		<br><br>

		The bones themselves are a matter of speculation. Some say they belonged to one of the spirit's descendants, or someone that it had once cursed.
	</span>
	<br><br>

	You get a running start, and throw the bones as far into the lake as you can. The sound of rippling water echoes around you. A gentle mist rises, enveloping the clearing.
	<br><br>

	You hear singing in a language you don't know. It's mesmerising. You take another step towards the lake automatically. The surface continues to ripple.
	A beautiful pale figure slowly emerges, cloaked in white. A necklace with large blue gemstones adorns its neck. It glides along the surface of the water towards you.
<<else>>
	You get a running start, and throw the bones as far into the lake as you can.
	<br><br>

	You wait. Nothing happens.
	<br><br>

	You turn to leave. You hear a voice.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Heed|Hopeless Cycle Wraith 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Wraith 2
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>

<<if $hc.trueEndAvailable>>
	"<span class="wraith">Clever gaoler, <<worldMale 'son' 'daughter'>> of the west moors. What yearning brings you before me?</span>"
	<br><br>

	It floats in a circle around you, inspecting you. It holds its necklace close.
	"<span class="wraith">Lend me yourself. Allow me to breathe the rich air through you. Gift me the warmth of your beating heart, and I will guide you to its desire.</span>"
	It reaches a pale hand towards you.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Take its hand|Hopeless Cycle Wraith 3]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Refuse|Hopeless Cycle Wraith Refuse]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	"<span class="wraith">Clever gaoler. This is not yet my story. Your heart is not ready.
	Feel all the struggles before you. Push against your fates until you've lost all hope. Only then, return to me, and repeat this act.</span>"
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Lake]]>><<pass 2>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>


:: Hopeless Cycle Wraith Refuse
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
"<span class="wraith">So be it.</span>"
<br><br>

It sinks back into the lake slowly, and the mist fades.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Lake]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Wraith 3
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<canvas-model-override "trauma" true>><<canvas-model-override "eyes_half" true>>
<<canvas-model-override "left_eye" "blue possessed">><<canvas-model-override "right_eye" "blue possessed">>
<<set $possessed to true>><<canvas-model-override "blink" false>>
<<set $control to 1>>
<<neckruined>><<neckwear "ivory necklace">>

You take its hand. It's cold, and starts to pass through you. It floats forward, embracing you and vanishing. Something hangs around your neck.
<br><br>

You stand frozen in place. Suddenly, your body takes a deep breath, looking upwards in bliss. The air tastes so sweet. You feel invigorated, as if waking up for the first time.
Your hands clench and open over and over.
<br><br>

<<if $prisonerBrands.includesAny("lower back", "left arm", "right arm", "left shoulder", "right shoulder")
	or $prisonerBrands.filter(brands => ["left leg", "left thigh", "left foot"].includes(brands)).length gte 2
	or $prisonerBrands.filter(brands => ["right leg", "right thigh", "right foot"].includes(brands)).length gte 2
	or between($prisonerBrands.length,1,2)>>
	<span class="red">You freeze.</span> Your mind ripples like water, and memories float to the surface.
	A searing brand pressed to flesh. Screams, both stifled and released. Beauty forever marked by a hubris made in divinity's image, guided by a cruel Hand.
	The sweet air now tastes bitter and stagnant.
	<br><br>

	Eventually, you exhale a haggard, wearied breath. "Writhing gaoler," your voice says. You place a hand over your chest.
	"Your heart sings to me beautifully. No one deserves to die in a cage.
	Your witch... <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> slips down the empty gullet. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> is not wholly consumed... <span class="red">but <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> will be.</span>"
	<br><br>

	<span class="nextLink"><<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Wraith Failure]]>><</link>></span>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<wearProp "whip" "khaki">>
	You exhale. "I understand," your voice says. You place a hand over your chest.
	"Your heart sings to me beautifully. No one deserves to die in a cage.
	Your witch... <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> slips down the empty gullet, yet <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> is not wholly consumed.
	What you seek lies through the eye of a needle. Fate does not favour you. There lies one path."
	<br><br>

	Your hand rests on your whip. Your body unclasps it and stretches it. "I will grant you a gift of knowledge. Arts and techniques lost to our faith. You will learn, and as you do, I will enlighten you on the path you must tread."
	<br><br>

	A pale arm separates from yours. A white tendril snakes along it, past the hand. It holds the tendril as you hold your whip. You have control of your arm again.
	"The arrow of time will be mere seconds from midnight. A distance your body cannot cross in time." The pale arm snaps the tendril. You snap your whip in the exact same way.
	"An extension of your body. Trust it, <span class="green">master it,</span> and distance will mean nothing."
	<br><br>

	It guides you through a dance of the whip. You know these movements. It's just testing your body. "<span class="blue">Heed my words. Remember them.</span> The slightest of missteps will have salvation slipping through your fingers."
	<br><br>

	<span class="nextLink"><<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Wraith 4]]>><</link>></span>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Wraith 4
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<set $control to 400>>

You follow its movements. You take your whip's end in your other hand, using it to start strikes from positions you've never seen. <<gwhip>>
<br><br>

"You must ensure <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> is strong enough. <span class="blue"><<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> body must be full of vitality.</span>"<br>
You lash a falling leaf out of the air. <<gwhip>><br>
<<if $hcChallenge.faithBlooms>>
	"<<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> hair, ever important to a witch, <span class="red">has been mangled</span>. You must make it more than beautiful to restore what was taken. <span class="purple">Accept <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> gift. Cleanse it. Bestow it back upon <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>.</span>"
<<else>>
	<span class="blue">"<<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> hair, ever important to a witch, must be beautiful."</span>
<</if>><br>
Your whip circles at your feet. You twirl and strike. Its rebound barely misses your ear. <<gwhip>><br>
"<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> is strengthened by your touch. <span class="blue">Take <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> hands</span>, so you may both bloom. <span class="blue">Your kiss, or your body in intimate union, will grant <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> power.</span>"<br>
You coil your whip, and make many quick strikes around you. <<prof whip 10>><<gwhip>><br>
"Two more gifts, you must give <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>. <span class="blue">Dress <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>,</span> a second skin to mask the lure of <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> body.
<span class="blue">Give <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> your name,</span> a promise to whisper."
<br><br>

It allows your body to rest for a moment. "Beware. <span class="red"><<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> heart is cold.</span> <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> will attempt to steal yours, if it wins <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> freedom.
<span class="blue">You must give it to <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> first, just before the fateful hour.</span>
Take heed. This will allow <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> to tear it from your chest without effort."
<br><br>

Your arms circle and stretch, preparing for more exertion.<br>
"You must burden your heart. Weighed down and offered as a final gift, it can't be stolen.
<span @class='$hcChallenge.faithBurden ? "" : "blue"'>Embrace the likeness of the expectant <<worldFemale 'mother' 'father'>>, until half of the burden rests on your shoulders.</span>"
<<if $hcChallenge.faithBurden>>
	<br><br>

	You tilt your head.<br>
	"<span class="gold">But you've already done that, haven't you?</span> Of course you have. Of course you have."
<</if>>
<br><br>

<span class="nextLink"><<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Wraith 5]]>><</link>></span>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Wraith 5
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<set $control to 800>>

You lash out with your whip twice in quick succession, carving a cross in the sand.
<br><br>

"<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> will be branded, in an attempt to seal the corruption inside. When <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> lies under the red moon, it will instead grow to bursting.
You must press this as an advantage. Your opponents are many. Only together can you stand against them. Heed."
<br><br>

You strike out twice more, making another cross.
<br><br>

"You must be precise with the flame in your hands.<br>
You may think it a mercy to scar <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> legs, to spare <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> pain.<br>
<span class="blue">Do not brand either more than once,</span> lest <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> stumble at the critical moment.<br>
<span class="blue">Do not brand the lower spine,</span> lest you sever <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> roots.<br>
<span class="blue">Do not brand either arm,</span> lest <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> claws become dull.<br>
<span class="blue">Do not brand either shoulder,</span> lest you clip <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> wings.<br>
Yet, <span class="blue">you must brand <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> at least thrice,</span> lest <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> be devoured by Auriga."
<br><br>

The word makes you shiver. Your eyes focus on a thick fallen tree branch on the far side of the clearing. You take a few steps back, measuring the distance.<br>
Another step. Not far enough yet.<br>
Half of another step. Perfect.<br>
"At last, <span class="blue">strike at the silver that binds <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>.</span> Let your strike toll midnight."
<br><br>

You take four rapid steps forward, beginning a strike on the second.<br>
You shift your body weight perfectly, fully extending your arm and flicking your wrist. Time slows down.<br>
The smallest of adjustments. The tip of your whip just barely makes contact.<br>
The explosive snap shatters the branch into pieces, and echoes throughout the forest. <<prof whip 20>><<gggwhip>>
<br><br>

<<if $prof.whip gte 1000>>
	<span class="green">"You are ready."</span>
<<else>>
	<span class="blue">"You must further hone your hand. Your strike must be perfect."</span>
<</if>>
<br>
The pale figure gently exits your body, leaving your limbs tingling. It smiles at you. "<span class="wraith">Best of fortunes, clever gaoler. May your hearts beat <span class="tentacle">As One</span>.</span>" It sinks back into the water. The mist fades away.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Lake]]>><<set $control to 1000>><<unset $possessed>><<set $hc.wraith to true>><<neckruined>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Wraith Failure
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<set $control to 0>>

You stretch your arm out. A pale arm separates from yours. Many white tendrils snake along it, past the hand. The pale arm gestures, and the tendrils swarm you.
<br><br>

"The flame you held was wielded with imperfection. You have sealed <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> fate."
<br><br>

<<if $prisonerBrands.includesAny("lower back", "left arm", "right arm", "left shoulder", "right shoulder")>>
	The tendrils press against your <<print formatList($prisonerBrands.filter(brands => ["lower back", "left arm", "right arm", "left shoulder", "right shoulder"].includes(brands)), "and")>>.<br>
<</if>>
"<span @class='$prisonerBrands.includes("lower back") ? "red" : ""'>With <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> lower spine branded,</span> <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> roots are severed.<br>
<span @class='$prisonerBrands.includesAny("left arm", "right arm") ? "red" : ""'>With either arm branded,</span> <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> claws become dull.<br>
<span @class='$prisonerBrands.includesAny("left shoulder", "right shoulder") ? "red" : ""'>With either shoulder branded,</span> <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> wings become clipped."
<br><br>

<<set _legColor to "">>
<<if $prisonerBrands.filter(brands => ["left leg", "left thigh", "left foot"].includes(brands)).length gte 2 or $prisonerBrands.filter(brands => ["right leg", "right thigh", "right foot"].includes(brands)).length gte 2>>
	<<set _legColor to "red">>
	The tendrils wrap around your <<print formatList($prisonerBrands.filter(brands => ["left leg", "right leg", "left thigh", "right thigh", "left foot", "right foot"].includes(brands)), "and")>>.<br>
<</if>>
"You may have thought it a mercy to scar <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> legs, to spare <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> pain.<br>
Yet, <span @class="_legColor">with either leg branded more than once,</span> <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> stumbles at the critical moment."
<br><br>

You count the tendrils. They touch your <<print formatList($prisonerBrands, "and")>>; <span class="blue"><<number $prisonerBrands.length>></span> in total.<br>
"Despite all this, <span @class='$prisonerBrands.length lt 3 ? "red" : ""'>if not branded at least thrice,</span> <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> is devoured by Auriga."
<br><br>

The pale figure gently exits your body, leaving your limbs tingling. "<span class="wraith">And now, you see. What you hoped for has already slipped through your fingers. There is no glory to be found here.</span>" It bows its head, and remains silent for a long time. "<span class="wraith">I am sorry.</span>"
<br><br>

It sinks back into the water. The mist fades away.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Lake]]>><<set $control to 999>><<unset $possessed>><<neckruined>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

/* Barracks */
:: Hopeless Cycle Quarters
<<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $bus to "quarters">>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
You are in the barracks on the second floor of the temple, where your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> make their home.
There are four large rooms surrounding the central hall.
<br><br>

<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
	The bunks are full and the rooms are silent save for an occasional snore.
<<elseif Time.dayState is "dawn">>
	Your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> are already up and active. It's too noisy to sleep.
<<elseif Time.dayState is "day">>
	Initiates are hard at work dusting and cleaning. It's too noisy to sleep.
<<elseif Time.dayState is "dusk">>
	Some of your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> are preparing for bed.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if _hcEvent is "blood">>
	A heavy hand rests on your shoulder. The Bishop's Hand looms before you. "<span class="red">It's time, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>.</span> Bring the witch up at once."
	<br><br>

	You enter the dungeon. There's no one to sanctify you on the way in. You suppose it's pointless since you'll be bringing <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> out anyways.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Enter <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell|Hopeless Cycle Blood Cell]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $hc.suspicion gte 100>>
	<span class="red">Everything goes dark as a sack is pulled over your head.</span> You're quickly struck in the gut, doubling you over. You're forced to your knees.
	<br><br>

	The last thing you feel is an impact against your head.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Ending E]]>><<pass 4 hours>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<set _water to hcItemCanReach("water", (water => water.dirty lt 2))>>
	<<set _waterTainted to hcItemCanReach("water", (waterT => waterT.dirty gte 2))>>
	<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
		You'll wake people up if you clean now.
		<br><br>
	<<elseif _water>>
		<<capture _water>>
			<<choreicon "sweep">><<link [[Clean barracks <<hcTimeTaskDisplay>>|Hopeless Cycle Quarters Clean]]>><<hcTimeTaskPass>><<hcSuspicion -3>><<hcWash _water>><<housekeeping 1 1000>><</link>><<ghousekeeping>><<hopelessCycleSus -1>>
		<</capture>>
		<br><br>
	<<else>>
		You need a bucket of water to clean the barracks.
		<<if _waterTainted>>
			A bucket of <span class="teal"><i>clean</i> water</span>.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	Your bunk is here.
	<br>
	<<bedicon>><<link [[Your bunk|Hopeless Cycle Bunk]]>><</link>>
	<br><br>

	<div id="hcItems" class="no-numberify"><<hopelessCycleItemLinks>></div>
	<b><u>Locations:</u></b><br>
	<<templeicon "cloister">><<link [[Passage to cloister (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Cloister]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Downstairs (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Temple]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Bunk
<<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $bus to "bed">>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
You are beside your bunk in the temple quarters. There's a rack for your armour and robes, and a small space behind a screen for dressing.
<br><br>

<<if ["dawn", "day"].includes(Time.dayState)>>
	<<set _noSleep to true>>
	It's too noisy to sleep right now.
	<br><br>
<</if>>

<<if _hcEvent is "blood">>
	A heavy hand rests on your shoulder. The Bishop's Hand looms before you. "<span class="red">It's time, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>.</span> Bring the witch up at once."
	<br><br>

	You enter the dungeon. There's no one to sanctify you on the way in. You suppose it's pointless since you'll be bringing <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> out anyways.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Enter <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell|Hopeless Cycle Blood Cell]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $hc.suspicion gte 100>>
	<span class="red">Everything goes dark as a sack is pulled over your head.</span> You're quickly struck in the gut, doubling you over. You're forced to your knees.
	<br><br>

	The last thing you feel is an impact against your head.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Ending E]]>><<pass 4 hours>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<if $worn.upper.name is "chain tunic">>
		<<if !_noSleep>>
			<<if hcItemLitTorch()>>
				<span class="red">You can't go to sleep while holding a lit torch.</span>
			<<else>>
				<<bedicon>><<link [[Change into your robes and get in bed (0:10)|Hopeless Cycle Bunk Bed]]>><<pass 10>><<hopelessCycleOutfit "robes">><<feetruined>><</link>>
			<</if>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<icon "clothes/monks-habit.png">><<link [[Change into your robes (0:10)|Hopeless Cycle Bunk]]>><<pass 10>><<hopelessCycleOutfit "robes">><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<if !_noSleep>>
			<<if hcItemLitTorch()>>
				<span class="red">You can't go to sleep while holding a lit torch.</span>
			<<else>>
				<<bedicon>><<link [[Get in bed|Hopeless Cycle Bunk Bed]]>><<feetruined>><</link>>
			<</if>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<set _armourIcon to clone(setup.clothes.upper[162])>>
		<<set _armourIcon.colour to "black">><<set _armourIcon.accessory_colour to "white">>
		<span class="clothes-black"><<clothingicon _armourIcon "upper">></span><<link [[Change into your armour (0:10)|Hopeless Cycle Bunk]]>><<pass 10>><<tiredness 4>><<hopelessCycleOutfit "armour">><</link>><<gtiredness>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<if $hairtype is "braid right">>
		<<mirroricon>><<link [[Unbraid your hair (0:05)|Hopeless Cycle Bunk]]>><<pass 5>>
			<<set $hairlength to 400>>
			<<set $hairlengthstage to "chest">>
			<<set $hairtype to "neat">>
			<<set $fringelength to 200>>
			<<set $fringelengthstage to "shoulder">>
			<<set $fringetype to "framed">>
			<<set $hairposition to "back">>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<<elseif $hairtype isnot "neat">>
		<<mirroricon>><<link [[Fix your hair (0:05)|Hopeless Cycle Bunk]]>><<pass 5>><<trauma -2>>
			<<set $hairlength to 400>>
			<<set $hairlengthstage to "chest">>
			<<set $hairtype to "neat">>
			<<set $fringelength to 200>>
			<<set $fringelengthstage to "shoulder">>
			<<set $fringetype to "framed">>
			<<set $hairposition to "back">>
		<</link>><<ltrauma>>
		<br>
	<<elseif $hairtype is "neat" and $prisonerEvents.includes("talkHairLet")>>
		<<mirroricon>><<link [[`Braid your hair the way $prisoner.name did (0:15)`|Hopeless Cycle Bunk]]>><<pass 15>>
			<<trauma -2>>
			<<set $hairtype to "braid right">>
			<<set $hairposition to "front">>
		<</link>><<ltrauma>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<br>

	You can stash items under your bed. They're unlikely to be found, but will arouse heavy suspicion if they are. Your bed will never be searched while you're sleeping in it.
	<br>
	<<if $hcItems.some(item => item.type is "sheets" and item.location is "bed") and !$hcChallenge.itemNoHide>>
		<span class="green">You've placed a folded bedsheet in front of your stashed items. They'll be even harder to find now.</span>
	<</if>>
	<div id="hcItems" class="no-numberify"><<hopelessCycleItemLinks>></div>
	<br>

	<<templeicon "quarters">><<link [[Step away|Hopeless Cycle Quarters]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Bunk Bed
<<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<set _witchblooms to hcItemCanReach("clutter", w => w.name === "witchblooms" && w.dirty gte 1)>>
<<if _witchblooms>>
	<<if _witchblooms.location is "held">>
		<<set _witchbloomsHeld to true>>
	<<elseif !$hc.daily.witchbloomMessage>>
		<<set $hc.daily.witchbloomMessage to true>>
		As you prepare for bed, <span class="pink">your hands twitch. They feel empty.</span>
		You look under your bed for the flowers. You want to hold them while you sleep, although you can't reason why.
		Perhaps they yearn for your purity.
		<br><br>

		<<capture _witchblooms>>
			<<link [[Take them|Hopeless Cycle Bunk Bed]]>><<set _witchblooms.location to "held">><</link>>
			<br>
		<</capture>>
		<<link [[Ignore them|Hopeless Cycle Bunk Bed]]>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<exit>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if $hcItems.some(item => item.location is "held" && item.name isnot "witchblooms")>>
	<<run $hcItems.filter(item => item.location is "held" && item.name isnot "witchblooms").forEach(item => item.location = "bed")>>
	<span class="blue">You stash your items under your bed,</span> before reciting your nightly prayers
	<<if _witchbloomsHeld>><span class="purple">with the flowers between your hands</span><</if>>
	and climbing in.
<<else>>
	You recite your nightly prayers
	<<if _witchbloomsHeld>><span class="purple">with the flowers between your hands</span><</if>>
	and climb into bed.
<</if>>
<br>

<<generateSleepLinks "Hopeless Cycle Sleep">>
<<link [[Climb out of bed|Hopeless Cycle Bunk]]>><<hopelessCycleOutfit "armour">><</link>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Sleep
<<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>>
<<sleep>><<effects>><<hopelessCycleEffects>><<set $hc.neverLeftDungeon to false>>
<<if _sleepinterrupt>>
	<<if $hc.bloodWake>>
		You shoot up out of bed, the red moonlight creeping in through the window.
	<<elseif $hc.daily.nightmare and $hc.nightBreakIn isnot "passed" and $hc.nightBreakIn isnot "end">>
		You dream of seeing <<print $prisoner.name>> in <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> cell. Someone in black robes is approaching <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> looks afraid.
		<br><br>

		<span class="red"><<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> calls to you for help.</span>
		<br><br>

		You shoot up from your bed.
	<<elseif $hc.daily.wake>>
		Your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> all get up for the day. It's impossible to sleep with the noise.
		<<if !$hc.daily.sermon and ["dawn","day"].includes(Time.dayState)>>
			<span class="blue">You should head to the cloister for the morning sermon.</span>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<set _witchblooms to hcItemHolding("clutter", w => w.name is "witchblooms")>>
	<<if _witchblooms>>
		<<if _witchblooms.progress and _witchblooms.progress gte 14>>
			<<set _witchblooms.name to "purified witchblooms">>
			<<set _witchblooms.nameText to "witchblooms <span class='gold'>(purified)</span>">>
			<<run delete _witchblooms.dirty>>
			<span class="green">The flowers are vibrant and full of life.</span><<llpurity>>
		<<elseif _witchblooms.progress>>
			<span class="teal">The flowers look healthier, but still sickly.</span><<llpurity>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	<<link [[Get up|Hopeless Cycle Bunk]]>><<hopelessCycleOutfit "armour">><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $hc.suspicion gte 100>>
	You open your eyes, but everything is still dark. <span class="red">There's something pulled over your head.</span> You're quickly struck in the gut, then dragged out of bed.
	<br><br>

	The last thing you feel is an impact against your head.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Ending E]]>><<pass 4 hours>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<if $nightmares gte 1 and $controlled is 0>>
		<<nightmareWake>>
	<<elseif $specialConditionForSpookySleep>>

	<<else>>
		You sleep soundly.
	<</if>>
	<<if $stress gte $stressmax>>
		<<set $stress -= 2000>>
		<<trauma 10>>
		<span class="red">Your stress level reached a peak while you slept and has since subsided, but at cost to your mental health.</span>
		<<lstress>><<gtrauma>>
		<<ruffleHair>>
		<<set $hairtype to "messy">>
		<<set $hairlength to 1000>>
		<<set $hairlengthstage to "feet">>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<set _witchblooms to hcItemHolding("clutter", w => w.name is "witchblooms")>>
	<<if _witchblooms>>
		<<if _witchblooms.progress and _witchblooms.progress gte 14>>
			<<set _witchblooms.name to "purified witchblooms">>
			<<set _witchblooms.nameText to "witchblooms <span class='gold'>(purified)</span>">>
			<<run delete _witchblooms.dirty>>
			<span class="green">The flowers are vibrant and full of life.</span><<llpurity>>
		<<elseif _witchblooms.progress>>
			<span class="teal">The flowers look healthier, but still sickly.</span><<llpurity>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<if _leak?.includes("bed")>>
		<<set _bucketOutput to _leak.filter(x => x is "bed").length gt 1 ? "buckets" : "bucket">>
		<span class="red">The water had leaked from your _bucketOutput while you slept.</span> You clean it up before anyone can notice.
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	<<link [[Get up|Hopeless Cycle Bunk]]>><<hopelessCycleOutfit "armour">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<set $phase to 0>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Quarters Clean
<<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

<<set _water to hcItemCanReach("water", (water => water.dirty lt 2))>>

You get to work scrubbing down the barracks. You clean the floors, some sheets, and some dirty clothing.
<br><br>

<i><span class="blue">Bedsheets can be used to conceal items inside of buckets. Any bucket with a bedsheet inside won't raise suspicion when entering the dungeon.</span></i>
<br><br>

<<if _hcEvent is "blood">>
	A heavy hand rests on your shoulder. The Bishop's Hand looms before you. "<span class="red">It's time, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>.</span> Bring the witch up at once."
	<br><br>

	You enter the dungeon. There's no one to sanctify you on the way in. You suppose it's pointless since you'll be bringing <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> out anyways.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Enter <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell|Hopeless Cycle Blood Cell]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $hc.suspicion gte 100>>
	<span class="red">Everything goes dark as a sack is pulled over your head.</span> You're quickly struck in the gut, doubling you over. You're forced to your knees.
	<br><br>

	The last thing you feel is an impact against your head.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Ending E]]>><<pass 4 hours>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $stress gte $stressmax>>
	<<hopelessCyclePassout>>
<<else>>
	<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
		You'll wake people up if you keep cleaning.
		<br>
	<<elseif _hcEvent is "blood">>
		There's no more time for cleaning.
		<br>
	<<elseif _water>>
		<<capture _water>>
			<<link [[Continue cleaning <<hcTimeTaskDisplay>>|Hopeless Cycle Quarters Clean]]>><<hcTimeTaskPass>><<hcSuspicion -3>><<hcWash _water>><<housekeeping 1 1000>><</link>><<ghousekeeping>><<hopelessCycleSus -1>>
		<</capture>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		Your water is too dirty to keep cleaning.
		<br>
	<</if>>

	<<set _loc to hcItemHasFreeHand() ? "held" : "quarters">>
	<<link [[Enough cleaning|Hopeless Cycle Quarters]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<capture _loc>>
		<<link [[Steal some bedsheets|Hopeless Cycle Quarters]]>><<run hcItemAdd({ type: "sheets", name: "bedsheets", location: _loc, origin: "quarters", dirty: 0, dirtyOnDrop: V.hcChallenge.itemDirty })>><<endevent>><<hcSuspicion 5>><</link>><<hopelessCycleSus 1>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Steal some clothes|Hopeless Cycle Quarters]]>><<run hcItemAdd({ type: "clothes", name: "robe", location: _loc, origin: "quarters", dirty: 0, dirtyOnDrop: V.hcChallenge.itemDirty })>><<endevent>><<hcSuspicion 5>><</link>><<hopelessCycleSus 1>>
		<br>
	<</capture>>
<</if>>


/* Prayer Room */
:: Hopeless Cycle Prayer Room
<<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $bus to "prayerroom">>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

<<if _hcEvent is "blood">>
	A heavy hand rests on your shoulder. The Bishop's Hand looms before you. "<span class="red">It's time, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>.</span> Bring the witch up at once."
	<br><br>

	You enter the dungeon. There's no one to sanctify you on the way in. You suppose it's pointless since you'll be bringing <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> out anyways.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Enter <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell|Hopeless Cycle Blood Cell]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $hc.handLocation is "prayerroom" and !$hc.daily.prayerWarning and $hcAction is "enter" and Time.hour lte 22 and Time.hour gte 6>>
	<<generateTemple 1>><<person1>>
	You approach the prayer room. One of your <<sister_npc>>s stops you. "The Bishop's Hand is in prayer."
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Enter anyways|Hopeless Cycle Prayer Room]]>><<endevent>><<set $hc.daily.prayerWarning to true>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Hopeless Cycle Temple]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You're in a small hexagonal room, the edges ringed with steps leading nowhere. A single window decorates each wall, far above. A cushion sits in the middle.
	<br><br>

	The air is thick with the smell of a sweet incense.
	<br><br>

	<<if $hc.handLocation is "prayerroom">>
		The Bishop's Hand stirs from <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> trance, but doesn't turn around to face you. "You better have a good reason for disturbing me, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>> Fayne." You're not sure how <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> knew it was you. <<stress 6>><<gstress>>
		<br><br>

		<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("raped") and !$prisonerEvents.includes("rapedReported")>>
			<<lockicon "unlock">><<link [[Tell the Hand that one of your brothers is tainted|Hopeless Cycle Prayer Report]]>><<set $prisonerEvents.pushUnique("rapedReported")>><</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Temple]]>><<hcSuspicion 2>><<pass 1>><</link>><<hopelessCycleSus 1>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<templeicon "pray">><<link [[Meditate <<hcTimeTaskDisplay>>|Hopeless Cycle Prayer]]>><<stress -6>><<willpower 2>><<hcTimeTaskPass>><</link>><<lstress>><<gwillpower>>
		<br><br>

		<div id="hcItems" class="no-numberify"><<hopelessCycleItemLinks>></div>
		<b><u>Locations:</u></b><br>
		<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Temple]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

<<unset $hcAction>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Prayer
<<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $bus to "prayerroom">>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

<<hallucinogen 60>>
You sit on the cushion, and pray. The incense makes you feel light and dizzy. <<ghallucinogens>>
<br><br>

<<if _hcEvent is "blood">>
	The door to the prayer room swings open. The Hand's silhouette looms. "<span class="red">It's time, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>.</span> Bring the witch up at once."
	<br><br>

	You enter the dungeon. There's no one to sanctify you on the way in. You suppose it's pointless since you'll be bringing <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> out anyways.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Enter <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell|Hopeless Cycle Blood Cell]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $hc.handLocation is "prayerroom">>
	The door to the prayer room swings open. The Bishop's Hand stands there. "Out," <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> commands.
	<br><br>
	<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("raped") and !$prisonerEvents.includes("rapedReported")>>
		<<lockicon "unlock">><<link [[Tell the Hand that one of your brothers is tainted|Hopeless Cycle Prayer Report]]>><<set $prisonerEvents.pushUnique("rapedReported")>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<templeicon "pray">><<link [[Meditate <<hcTimeTaskDisplay>>|Hopeless Cycle Prayer]]>><<stress -6>><<willpower 2>><<hcTimeTaskPass>><</link>><<lstress>><<gwillpower>>
	<br><br>

	<div id="hcItems" class="no-numberify"><<hopelessCycleItemLinks>></div>
<</if>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Temple]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Prayer Report
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<span class="narration">The gaoler could not let the witch's defilement go unpunished. Justice was not something to be picked and chosen.</span>
<br><br>

You tell <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> that one of your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters'>> violated your prisoner. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> tenses up.
<br><br>

You stand in deafening silence for a long time, before <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> finally stands.
<br><br>

"And how, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>, do you know that?"
<br><br>

You explain everything in excruciating detail. You're not even meaning to. The words flow from your mouth against your will.
<br><br>

<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> seems to get angrier with every word you say, until <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> shoulders finally fall. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> smiles at you. Warmly. It makes you uncomfortable.
<br><br>

"It's hard to lie in a place so close to heaven. Good work, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>." <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> laughs, and pats you on the shoulder. "This presents a contamination risk. We will do an emergency inspection. Come." <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> leads you out of the prayer room, rings the confessional's bell loudly seven times, and walks with you to the cloister. <<hcSuspicion -50>><<hopelessCycleSus -3>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Prayer Report 2]]>><<pass 30>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Prayer Report 2
<<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $bus to "cloister">>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

Your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>> all line up in front of you and the Bishop's Hand in the cloister.
<br><br>

<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
	Many of them yawn, their posture slacking until the Hand's gaze falls upon them.
<<else>>
	They all stand at attention. Many look nervous.
<</if>>
<br><br>

The Hand whispers in your ear, asking for clarifying details. With each question, some of the crowd are permitted to leave, until there's only six <<worldMale 'monks' 'nuns'>> left.
<br><br>

They're each given a chastity examination. Out of them, two fail. The Hand grabs them each by a shoulder, and looks back to you. "Are you certain it was only one?" They both look terrified.
<br><br>

<<link [[Yes|Hopeless Cycle Prayer Report 3]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[No|Hopeless Cycle Prayer Report 3]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Prayer Report 3
<<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>><<set $bus to "guardhouse">>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

<<if $phase is 1>>
	You nod your head.
<<else>>
	You shake your head.
<</if>>
The Hand huffs. "Then we have no choice." <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> starts to guide them both to the dungeon. You follow, along with an entire regiment of confessors.
<br><br>

You're led to <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell. The hand walks in with both of the suspects. <<print $prisoner.name.toUpperFirst()>> looks up, shying away.
<br><br>

"Witch," the Hand spits. "One of the faithful has been tainted by your touch."
<br><br>

<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> blinks at <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>, not seeming to understand <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>. However, <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> eye falls upon the <<worldMale 'monk' 'nun'>> on the right. <<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> stare is pointedly hateful. That's enough indication for the Hand.
<br><br>

<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> shoves the other <<worldMale 'monk' 'nun'>> out of the cell, into the waiting arms of the confessors. "You must be purified," they say. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> seems relieved to only be facing the normal punishment.
<br><br>

The guilty <<worldMale 'monk' 'nun'>> sneers, struggling in the Hand's grasp. "This is an outrage. I should not be punished for bringing this whore closer to God!" <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>>'s silenced as the Hand punches <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> directly in the face, sending <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> to the ground.
<br><br>

The Hand crouches, looking <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> in the eyes as <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> clutches <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> bleeding nose. "You have transgressed, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>. You have either given the witch what <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> needs to invite the Dark Elk... or have taken that taint into yourself, without sanction, and have become a contamination risk." <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> rips a pouch from <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> belt, and dumps powder on the ground in front of the door.
"You will be the vessel for that taint. You will purge. You will repent, and be forgiven." <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> nods to you, signaling for you to approach.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Prayer Report 4]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Prayer Report 4
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>><<wearProp "whip" "khaki">>
<span class="narration">The witch was treated like a dog on a leash.</span>
<br><br>

The Hand holds out a silk cord for you to take. You grab it, wrapping it around <<print $prisoner.name>>'s neck. You've enacted this kind of punishment before. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> then exits the cell, locking the door, but remains standing there. Watching.
<br><br>

You look at your prisoner. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> eyes the <<worldMale 'monk' 'nun'>> angrily, <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> hands scraping against <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> shackles. The Hand licks <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> lips, and motions for you to unlock <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> shackles. You do so. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> falls forwards, <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> hands digging into the stone as <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> grey eye pierces through the <<worldMale 'monk' 'nun'>>.
<br><br>

<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> tries to stand. In one swift motion, you unclasp your whip and lash <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> in the leg. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> tumbles back down, and you give <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> a second lash for good measure.
<br><br>

<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> pushes <<worldMale 'himself' 'herself'>> back against the wall. "P-please, your grace, have mercy!"
<br><br>

The Hand laughs. "I'm not the one you should be asking." <<print $prisoner.name.toUpperFirst()>> drags <<worldFemale 'herself' 'himself'>> forwards. You walk forwards with <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>.
<br><br>

The <<worldMale 'monk' 'nun'>>, the rapist, the defiler, the oathbreaker looks to you, pleading. Your fist clenches around the cord.
<br><br>

<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> nearly reaches <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>, <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> left arm and hand becoming black. <<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> fingers elongating, sharpening. The antler on <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> head pulsing.
<br><br>

<<link [[Show mercy|Hopeless Cycle Prayer Report 5]]>><<set $phase to 1>><<pass 15>><</link>>
<br>
<<if $sadism_level gte 2 and ($prisoner.love gte 45 or $prisoner.love gte 30 and $prisonerEvents.includes("comfort"))>>
	<<link [[Release the cord|Hopeless Cycle Ending C]]>><</link>><<note "Sadist" "purple">>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<insufficientStat "custom" "to release the cord" "purple" "sadistic">>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Prayer Report 5
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>><<set $hc.daily.enteredDungeon to true>>
<<if $hc.gameOver>>
	<<set $hc.gameOver to false>>
<</if>>
<span class="narration">Despite the <<worldMale 'monk' 'nun'>>'s crime, the gaoler and the witch did not lose themselves. Make no mistake, <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> was punished, but the punishment did not exceed the crime. Such was the duty of a gaoler.</span>
<br><br>

<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> lunges at <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>. You tighten the cord just enough to force <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> to hold back. You have no intention to let <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> leave unpunished, but you have enough kindness left in your heart to ensure <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> isn't broken.
<br><br>

<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> gets <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> hands around <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>. In <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> current state, <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>>'s strong enough to hold <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> down, to strike <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>, to make sure that everything <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> does hurts. <<worldMale 'His' 'Her'>> punishment is gruelling. You pull <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> back each time you feel <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>>'s going too far.
<br><br>

After fifteen minutes, you pull <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> off of <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>. The Hand looks pleased.
<br><br>

The confessors re-enter the cell to retrieve the <<worldMale 'monk' 'nun'>>, who sobs and groans in pain. The Hand nods to you. "Continue as you will, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>." They all leave the dungeon. <<set $hc.handLocation to "prayerroom">>
<br><br>

<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("comfort")>>
	You start to pull <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> back to the wall. <<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> arms suddenly wrap around you, bringing you to the ground.
	<br><br>

	You struggle, worried that <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>>'s still seeking further purging. You stop when you realise that <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>>'s simply embracing you. <<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> head presses into your chest, and a warm smile is across <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> lips. <<set $prisoner.love += 10>><<hcPrisonerHealth 10>><<gglove>>
	<br><br>

	The usual chill and weakness from <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> touch is absent, if only for a moment. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> releases you before it comes back.
<<else>>
	You pull <<print $prisoner.name>> back to the wall and re-secure <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> manacles. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> looks satisfied. <<set $prisoner.love += 2>><<hcPrisonerHealth 10>><<hopelessCycleLove 1>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Cell]]>><<endevent>><<set $hc.daily.patrol to true>><<set $prisoner.state to "awake">><</link>>
<br>


:: Hopeless Cycle Passout
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

<span class="narration">
	In the wake of the gaoler's fainting spell, many items had been found, returned or burned as needed.
	<<if $witchItems>>
		<<unset $witchItems>>
		This included several items in the witch's cell, and on <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> person.
	<</if>>
</span>
<br><br>

<<if $bus is "cell">>
	You awaken feeling warm. Something is on top of you.
	<br><br>

	You open your eyes, and see a single grey one staring back. <<print $prisoner.name.toUpperFirst()>> quickly crawls back to the wall away from you.
	<br><br>

	You feel strange, but <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> looks a little more healthy. <<purity -200>><<lllpurity>><<hcPrisonerHealth 3>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Cell]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<set $location to "old_temple">><<set $outside to 1>><<set $bus to "garden">>
	You awaken to some water being poured on your head. You open your eyes and try to push away the source.
	<br><br>

	You look around. You're in the temple's garden, surrounded by some of your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>>. One holds a bucket.
	<<if $hc.suspicionRevealed>>
		"I'm telling you, <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>>'s bewitched!"
		<br><br>

		One of them helps you stand. "We'll have to report this to the bishop, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>." <<hcSuspicion 15>><<hopelessCycleSus 3>>
	<<else>>
		<<set $hc.suspicionRevealed to true>>
		"<<worldMale 'Brother' 'Sister'>> Fayne, what's going on?" one asks. "This is not like you. We grow concerned."
		<br><br>

		Another one of them pushes in. "Some in the order fear you've been bewitched. For your sake, prove us wrong. Soon." The crowd disperses.
		<br><br>

		<span class="narration">The Bishop's Hand and <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> confessors had been watching the gaoler. Now that <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> knew this, <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> would be more aware of what actions would make them suspicious.</span>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Garden]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Shortcut
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<set _comingFrom to "Hopeless Cycle " + $bus.toLocaleUpperFirst()>>
<<set _goingTo to "Hopeless Cycle " + ($bus is "disposal" ? "Forest" : "Disposal")>>

You walk through the dank cave by the light of your torch, occasionally crouching as the ceiling bares down.
<<if !$hcChallenge.forestNoShortcut>>
	It's cold and uncomfortable, but you eventually emerge
	<<if $bus is "disposal">>
		deep into the forest.
	<<else>>
		in the temple's disposal channel.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|_goingTo]]>><</link>>
<<elseif $hc.shortcutCount is undefined>>
	<<set $hc.shortcutCount to 0>><<set $shortcut to {lost: 0}>>
	It's cold and uncomfortable, and the cave winds around in ways that almost feel cyclical. You can't tell if you're making any progress.
	<br><br>

	You turn a corner and bump your head against what seems to be thin air. Confused, you place your hand forward. <span class="blue">A wall of glass blocks your way.</span> You can advance no further.
	<br><br>

	You turn around. <span class="red">The cave branches off in several directions.</span> You can't even tell which way you came from.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Follow the first path (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Lost]]>><<pass 1>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Follow the second path (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Lost]]>><<pass 1>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Follow the third path (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Lost]]>><<pass 1>><<set $phase to 3>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Follow the fourth path (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Lost]]>><<pass 1>><<set $phase to 4>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $hc.shortcutCount is 0>>
	It's cold and uncomfortable, but you eventually emerge...
	<<if $bus is "disposal">>
		in the temple's disposal channel.
	<<else>>
		deep in the forest.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	You look behind you. The path branches off in several familiar directions. You hear a screech of glass rubbing against glass. <span class="purple">You must make an offering <<= $bus is "forest" ? "at the disposal channel" : "">> before you are permitted to pass.</span>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Return|_comingFrom]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<set $hc.shortcutCount-->>
	It's cold and uncomfortable, but you eventually emerge
	<<if $bus is "disposal">>
		deep into the forest.
	<<else>>
		in the temple's disposal channel.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<if $hc.shortcutCount gte 1>>
		You feel a pair of eyes watching you, but hear nothing. You may travel this path <span class="blue"><<number $hc.shortcutCount>> more <<pluralise $hc.shortcutCount "time">></span>.
	<<else>>
		You feel a pair of eyes watching you, and hear a piercing screech of glass rubbing against glass. <span class="red">You no longer have permission to travel this path,</span> and must make another offering if you wish to pass.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|_goingTo]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Lost
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>

<span class="narration">
	<<if $phase is 0>>
		The gaoler doubled back along the path <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> had just walked.
	<<elseif $phase is 10>>
		The gaoler examined the walls. As long as <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> could see, <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> could keep track of which paths <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>>'d been down.
	<<else>>
		The gaoler travelled along the <<print ordinalWritten($phase)>> path <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> saw.
	<</if>>
</span>
<br><br>

<<if $shortcut.lost gte 5>>
	<<pain -2>>
	<<set _goingTo to $bus is "disposal" ? "forest" : "disposal channel">>
	<<set $shortcut.item to $hcItems.filter(item => item.location is "held" and item.type isnot "torch")[0]>>
	<<if $shortcut.item?.type is "container" and $hcItems.filter(x => x.type is "water" and x.location is $shortcut.item.containerID).length>>
		<<set $shortcut.itemName to "a bucket of water">>
	<<elseif !$shortcut.item or $shortcut.item.persists>>
		<<set $shortcut.itemName to "a roll of bandages">>
	<<else>>
		<<set $shortcut.itemName to hcItemName($shortcut.item)>>
	<</if>>
	<<set $shortcut.itemName to $shortcut.itemName.substr($shortcut.itemName.indexOf(" ") + 1)>>
	You run into another glass wall. You step back and try to look through it.
	<br><br>

	No. It's not a wall. It's a mirror.
	<br><br>

	You look into the mirror. A gaoler holding a <<= $shortcut.itemName>> and <span class="orange">a lit torch</span> looks back.
	Behind your reflection, in the mirror, <span class="green">you see the <<= $bus is "forest" ? "disposal channel" : "forest">></span> you were intending to go to.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Reach out|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Mirror]]>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Turn around and go to the _goingTo|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Mirror]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<switch $shortcut.lost>>
		<<case 0>>
			You've heard rumours of these tricks. The path is defying you because you believe it is.
			<br><br>
			You scratch the wall of the cave with your torch's handle as you walk. The scraping doesn't sound like stone.
		<<case 1>>
			You hear a rapid rattling and thumping approach from some unknown path. You swing your torch around you, but see nothing.
		<<case 2>>
			<span class="red">Your <<= $hcItems.filter(torch => torch.type is "torch" and torch.state is "lit" and torch.location is "held").length is 1 ? "torch goes" : "torches go">> out!</span>
			You feel blindly for the wall. You can't feel any markings.
			<<run $hcItems.filter(torch => torch.type is "torch" and torch.state is "lit" and torch.location is "held").forEach(torch => {torch.state = "snuffed"})>>

			<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
		<<case 3>>
			You attempt to stay the course, believing there is only one path. You run into a wall.
			<<stress 6>><<pain 2>><<gstress>><<gpain>>
		<<case 4>>
			You run, directionless and lost. Nothing seems real.
			<<stress 12>><<ggstress>>
	<</switch>>
	<<set $shortcut.lost++>>
	<br><br>

	More paths branch off ahead.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Try to backtrack (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Lost]]>><<pass 1>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Follow the first path (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Lost]]>><<pass 1>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Follow the second path (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Lost]]>><<pass 1>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Follow the third path (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Lost]]>><<pass 1>><<set $phase to 3>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Follow the fourth path (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Lost]]>><<pass 1>><<set $phase to 4>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Follow the fifth path (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Lost]]>><<pass 1>><<set $phase to 5>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<if $shortcut.lost gte 2>>
		<<link [[Follow the sixth path (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Lost]]>><<pass 1>><<set $phase to 6>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<if $shortcut.lost gte 3>>
			<<link [[Follow the seventh path (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Lost]]>><<pass 1>><<set $phase to 7>><</link>>
			<br>
			<<if $shortcut.lost gte 4>>
				<<link [[Follow the eighth path (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Lost]]>><<pass 1>><<set $phase to 8>><</link>>
				<br>
				<<link [[Follow the ninth path (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Lost]]>><<pass 1>><<set $phase to 9>><</link>>
				<br>
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<<if between($shortcut.lost,1,2)>>
		<<link [[Look for paths with marked walls (0:01)|Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Lost]]>><<pass 1>><<set $phase to 10>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Shortcut Mirror
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<set _goingTo to $bus is "disposal" ? "forest" : "disposal channel">>
<<set _comingFrom to $bus is "disposal" ? "disposal channel" : "forest">>
<<set _comingFromLink to "Hopeless Cycle " + $bus.toLocaleUpperFirst()>>
<<set $hcItems.filter(torch => torch.type is "torch" and ["snuffed","burnt"].includes(torch.state) and torch.location is "held")[0].state to "lit">>
<<wearProp "torch">>

<<if $phase is 0>>
	You step forward, up to the mirror. After a slight delay, your reflection does the same.
<<else>>
	You turn around, hoping to see the _goingTo behind you. All you see is more paths into the darkness. You turn back around.
	<br><br>

	Your reflection steps forward, up to the mirror. After a slight delay, you do the same.
<</if>>
<br><br>

The reflection holds <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> lit torch up. Feeling somewhat foolish, you raise your snuffed torch to match the movement.
<br><br>

<span class="green">Your torch catches alight.</span>
<br><br>

The reflection turns, letting go of <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> torch. It remains in midair.
<<if $shortcut.itemName is "bucket of water">>
	<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> takes <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> bucket of water and empties it out to the side.
<<else>>
	<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> takes <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> <<print $shortcut.itemName>> and throws it to the side, as hard as <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> can.
<</if>>
After a moment, <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> picks up <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> torch, turns around and continues on to the _goingTo.
<br><br>

<span class="blue">The mirror cracks.</span> The reflection freezes, the flame's flickering going entirely still. With a horrific sound, the mirror shatters. Behind the mirror is the _comingFrom.
<br><br>

<span class="purple">You may not traverse the shortcut without leaving an offering.</span> Dispose of items in the disposal channel to gain access. Tainted items are considered higher-value offerings.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|_comingFromLink]]>><<unset $shortcut>><</link>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Blood Cell Late
<<set $location to "old_temple">><<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<set $bus to "barracks">>

<<if $worn.upper.name isnot "chain tunic">>
	You head to the barracks and change into your armour.
	<<hopelessCycleOutfit "armour">>
	<br><br>
<</if>>

The Bishop's Hand finds you. "You're late. <span class="red">It's time, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>.</span> Bring the witch up at once."
<br><br>

You enter the dungeon. There's no one to sanctify you on the way in. You suppose it's pointless since you'll be bringing <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> out anyways.
<br><br>

<<link [[Enter <<print $prisoner.name>>'s cell|Hopeless Cycle Blood Cell]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Blood Cell
<<set $location to "old_temple">><<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<set $bus to "cell">>
<<hopelessCycleOutfit "armour">><<canvas-model-override "mouth" "neutral">><<tiredness -12>>
<<run $hcItems.filter(items => items.type isnot "prisoner" and items.location isnot "prisoner").forEach(item => {hcItemRemove(item)})>>

<<if $phase is 1>>
	You look down to <<= $prisoner.name>>.
<<elseif $phase is 2>>
	You just keep holding <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>. You know it can't last.
<<else>>
	You enter <<= $prisoner.name>>'s cell.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if $prisoner.state is "catatonic">>
	<span class="red"><<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> barely reacts to your presence. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> doesn't even know what's coming in <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> catatonic state.</span>
	Perhaps that's for the best. Still, part of you wonders if you should have ensured <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> was healthier.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Blood Pick Up]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $prisoner.harmed gte Math.floor($prisoner.love / 6)>>
	<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> glares at you, not desiring any of your pity. You both know this is it.
	<br><br>

	You release the chain that holds <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> manacles to the wall and pick <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> up. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> doesn't struggle, but refuses to look at you.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Blood Carry]]>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> looks up to you with worry. You both know this is it.
	<br><br>

	<<if $prisoner.love gte 60>>
		Your mind searches for an alternative. It finds none. You don't want to do this, but your faith demands it.
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	<<if $prisoner.love gte 80 and ($prisonerEvents.includes("kiss") or $prisonerEvents.includesAll("legs", "face", "talkMagic", "talkName", "washHair", "spendNight", "sex"))>>
		<<link [[Give <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> your heart|Hopeless Cycle Blood Love]]>><<set $prisoner.love += 10>><</link>><<hopelessCycleLove 3>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<link [[Reassure <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>|Hopeless Cycle Blood Comfort]]>><<set $prisoner.love++>><</link>><<hopelessCycleLove 1>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Pick <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> up|Hopeless Cycle Blood Pick Up]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Blood Love
<<set _thermoDisable to true>>
<<set $prisonerEvents.pushUnique("love")>>

You tell <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> that everything will be alright.<br>
You tell <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> that <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>>'ll be redeemed, and that once this is over, you'll still take care of <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>.<br>
You tell <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> that you won't leave <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> side.<br>
You tell <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> that you don't care if physical contact with <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> drains you.<br>
You tell <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> no one is beyond forgiveness, and you've already forgiven <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>.<br>
You ask <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> to forgive you for the way you treated <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> at first. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> nods, taking your hands.
<br><br>

You tell <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> that your heart is <<worldFemale 'hers' 'his'>>. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> embraces you and nods into your shoulder.
<br><br>

Comforting lies. Lies you both wish were true.
<br><br>

At least the very last part was the truth.
<br><br>

You release the chain that holds <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> manacles to the wall and pick <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> up. <<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> arms wrap around you for stability, and <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> tries to hold you as tightly as <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> can.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Blood Carry]]>><<set $phase to 3>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Blood Comfort
<<set _thermoDisable to true>>

You tell <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> that everything will be alright. It's a comforting lie, one <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> doesn't believe.
<br><br>

You release the chain that holds <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> manacles to the wall and pick <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> up. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> holds on to you tightly.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Blood Carry]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Blood Pick Up
<<set _thermoDisable to true>>

You release the chain that holds <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> manacles to the wall and pick <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> up. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> doesn't struggle.
<br><br>

<<link [[Pick <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> up|Hopeless Cycle Blood Carry]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Blood Carry
<<set $outside to 0>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<set $bus to "cloister">>
<<set $hc.forcedMove to true>><<run delete $hc.endingETimer>>
<<canvas-model-override "mouth" "neutral">><<canvas-model-override "eyes_half" true>>
<<canvas-model-override "arm_left" "none">><<canvas-model-override "arm_right" "none">>

<<set _witchClothes to $hcItems.find(clothes => clothes.type is "clothes" and clothes.location is "prisoner")?.name>>
<<hopelessCycleBrandings>>

<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("talkHairBlooms")>>
	<<set $hc.witchHair to "hair-flowers">>
<<elseif $prisonerEvents.includes("talkHair")>>
	<<set $hc.witchHair to "hair-braid">>
<<elseif $prisonerEvents.includes("washHair")>>
	<<set $hc.witchHair to "hair-clean">>
<<else>>
	<<set $hc.witchHair to "hair-dirty">>
<</if>>

<<if $prisoner.state is "catatonic" or $phase lte 1>>
	<<set _left_arm to "left-arm">>
	<<if _witchClothes is "robe">>
		<<set _clothes_left_arm to "robe-left-arm">>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<set _left_arm to "left-arm-alt">>
	<<if _brandings.left_arm>>
		<<run delete _brandings.left_arm>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

<<if $prisoner.bandagesOn>>
	<<set _bandages to "bandages">>
<</if>>

<<if _witchClothes is "robe">>
	<<set _clothes to "robe">>
<<elseif _witchClothes is "bloodstained sack" or _witchClothes is "torn vegetable sack">>
	<<set _clothes to "sack">>
<</if>>

<<set $follower to {
	name: "witchprisoner",
	base: "base",
	left_arm: _left_arm,
	clothes_left_arm: _clothes_left_arm,
	hair: $hc.witchHair,
	under_clothes: _bandages,
	clothes: _clothes,
	writing_right_cheek: _brandings.right_cheek,
	writing_chest: _brandings.chest,
	writing_left_arm: _brandings.left_arm,
	writing_right_arm: _brandings.right_arm,
	writing_right_shoulder: _brandings.right_shoulder,
	writing_right_thigh: _brandings.right_thigh,
	writing_right_leg: _brandings.right_leg,
	writing_right_foot: _brandings.right_foot
}>>
<<if $hcChallenge.faithBlooms>>
	<<set $follower.hair += "-challenge-faithBlooms">>
<</if>>

<<run Time.timeTravel(new DateTime(1390, 5, 31, 22, 0))>>
<<set Weather.set("clear", true, 1000)>>
<span class="narration">To this day, the temple puts special emphasis on the last day of each month. It is unclear when this tradition started, but it has been around for centuries.</span>
<br><br>

You carry <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> from the cell, towards the dungeon stairs.
<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("love")>>
	You briefly look back to the entrance of the disposal channel. You think about your chances running. Abandoning it all for <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>.
	<br><br>

	You hear your name called from the top of the stairs. A priest is looking at you. It's too late.
<</if>>
You begin the climb.
<br><br>

You emerge to a line of masked, black-robed confessors on either side of the dungeon entrance. They create a corridor for you to walk down.
Behind them is all of your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters' 'brothers and sisters'>>, trying to get a look at you.
<br><br>

The Bishop stands at the end, with the Hand standing besides. They both nod to you, turn, and begin to walk.
You slowly follow. The black-robed priests and priestesses file in line behind you in sets of two as you pass them.
<br><br>

<<if $phase is 0>>
	<<= $prisoner.name.toUpperFirst()>>'s hateful gaze dissuades anyone from watching you for too long.
<<elseif $phase is 1>>
	<<= $prisoner.name.toUpperFirst()>> draws curious stares from the many members of the flock that haven't seen <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> yet.
<<elseif $phase is 2>>
	<<= $prisoner.name.toUpperFirst()>> draws curious stares from the many members of the flock that haven't seen <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> yet. Some of them look at you with curiosity too, seeing how <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>>'s holding on to you.
<<else>>
	Your siblings stare at you and <<= $prisoner.name>> curiously. Some audibly comment on how you're holding each other, whispering 'bewitched' and 'seduced.' Many say prayers for you.
<</if>>
<br><br>

As you cross the threshold to the garden, another pair of confessors holding wooden rods unfurl a silken black cloth above you, sheltering the two of you from the red moonlight.
They walk by your side in-step, the silk trailing on the ground behind you.
<br><br>

<<link [[Walk|Hopeless Cycle Blood Garden]]>><<pass 45>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Blood Garden
<<set $location to "forest">><<set $outside to 1>><<set _thermoDisable to true>><<set $bus to "forest">>
<span class="narration">
	Out and out they went, across the temple's grounds, to the forest. The Bishop, and <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> Hand. The gaoler, and the witch.
	Two dozen confessors, and many more members of the flock. Marching in procession behind the tainted pair.
	<br><br>

	The two frontmost confessors diligently kept the gaoler and the witch sheltered from the moon.
</span>
<br><br>

A shadowed line crossing the temple grounds, with you at the front. Those behind you perfectly match your pace.
The faithful are linked by divine purpose, moving as one.
<br><br>

You can't say when you cross the threshold from the grounds to the forest. The separation was never clear.
The ground is a patchwork of pitch-black shadow and bright red moonlight. You march onwards.
<br><br>

You hear a heartbeat growing in volume and speed.
<<if $prisoner.state is "catatonic">>
	<<= $prisoner.name.toUpperFirst()>> hangs limp in your arms.
<<elseif $phase is 2 or $phase is 3>>
	<<= $prisoner.name.toUpperFirst()>> clings to you tighter.
<<else>>
	<<= $prisoner.name.toUpperFirst()>>'s breathing becomes laboured. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> grips your tunic.
<</if>>
<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("legs")>>
	You wonder how disorienting it must feel to be carried in <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> condition.
	<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> can't feel your left arm under <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> legs. It must feel like <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>>'s half-floating.
<</if>>
<<if $prisoner.state isnot "catatonic" and $phase gte 1>>
	<<set $follower.base to "base-alt">>
	<<if $follower.clothes is "robe">>
		<<set $follower.clothes to "robe-alt">>
	<<elseif $follower.clothes is "sack">>
		<<set $follower.clothes to "sack-alt">>
	<</if>>
	<<if $follower.under_clothes>>
		<<set $follower.under_clothes to "bandages-alt">>
	<</if>>
	<<if $follower.writing_chest>>
		<<set $follower.writing_chest to "brand-chest-alt">>
	<</if>>
	<<if $follower.writing_right_arm>>
		<<set $follower.writing_right_arm to "brand-right-arm-alt">>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

You take a deep breath as the clearing, and the altar, come into view.
<br><br>

<<link [[Approach|Hopeless Cycle Blood Altar]]>><<pass 45>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Blood Altar
<<set _thermoDisable to true>>
<span class="narration">
	This part of the tale always interested me most. Even across retellings, the detail of an altar in the forest remains constant.
	Could it still be out there?
</span>
<br><br>

The Bishop and <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> Hand take their spot at the head of the altar, each holding up a hand to signal you to stop.
You do so, a few steps away from the altar. The silk-bearers do as well, but the rest of the procession files around you.
<br><br>

The altar is a solid rectangular slab of stone, intricately carved on the edges. Parts have been deformed by the elements.
The first two confessors to reach it affix a small silver blade to each lower corner, before walking to opposite ends.
<br><br>

The rest of the confessors slowly pass the altar in two lines, one for each side.
As they do, <span class="red">they run their hands along the blades.</span> They're held outstretched, dripping their blood onto the altar.
<br><br>

By the time every member has passed, the altar has become soaked in faithful blood. Finally, they form a circle around the clearing.
The Bishop motions for you to approach.
<br><br>

The silk-bearers walk with you to the altar, spreading the silk above you to shade it.
<br><br>

<<link [[Lay <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> down|Hopeless Cycle Blood Altar 2]]>><<unset $follower>><<canvas-model-override "clear">><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Blood Altar 2
<<set _thermoDisable to true>>
<<canvas-model-override "mouth" "neutral">>
<span class="narration">A blood-steeped altar. A blood red moon. Silver to prevent transmission. All in accordance with their scripture.</span>
<br><br>

You gently lay <<= $prisoner.name>> down on the altar.
<<if $prisoner.state is "catatonic">>
	<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> lays limp as the Bishop's Hand binds <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> manacles to the altar at <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> sides.
<<elseif $phase is 0>>
	<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> tries pushing away from you, but is quickly restrained by the Bishop's Hand. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> binds <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> manacles to the altar at <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> sides.
<<elseif $phase is 1>>
	<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> doesn't put up a fight. The Bishop's Hand binds <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> manacles to the altar at <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> sides.
<<elseif $phase is 2>>
	<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> clings to your tunic for just a moment before releasing you in kind. Your hands linger on each other briefly. The Bishop's Hand binds <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> manacles to the altar at <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> sides.
<<else>>
	You try to move your arms away, but <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>>'s still holding on to you. <<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> face is buried in your chest. You continue to hold <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> for a moment, before you feel <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> being pulled away by the Bishop's Hand.
	<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> grips your arm, not wanting to let go, but <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> can't hope to fight against <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> binds <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> manacles to the altar at <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> sides.
<</if>>
A silver collar is put around <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> neck, too.
<br><br>

<<if $hcItems.some(clothes => clothes.type is "clothes" and clothes.location is "prisoner")>>
	<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> then cuts away <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> clothes,<<if $prisoner.bandagesOn>> followed by <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> bandages,<</if>> leaving <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> wholly naked and exposed for all to see.
<<elseif $prisoner.bandagesOn>>
	<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> then cuts away <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> bandages, leaving <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> wholly naked and exposed for all to see.
<<else>>
	<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> lies wholly naked and exposed for all to see.
<</if>>
Some of the flock avert their gaze, while others become lost in <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> supernatural allure.
<br><br>

"You who bears <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> taint," comes the aged voice of the Bishop, directed at you.
<<if $prisoner.state is "catatonic">>
	"I am not impressed. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> barely clings to life. You should have seen to it that <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> would be aware for <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> final punishment." <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> shakes <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> head. "No matter.
<<elseif $phase is 3>>
	"You have done well watching over this servant of the Dark Elk. However, I worry that you feel sympathy for <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>. No matter.
<<else>>
	"You have done well watching over this servant of the Dark Elk. You will be honoured for your service and sacrifice.
<</if>>
Judgement awaits. Spill your blood upon <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>."
<br><br>

You prick your fingers with your silver dagger. You squeeze each with your other hand to tease forth fresh blood, and run them down <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> chest between <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> breasts.
<<if $prisonerBrands.includes("chest")>>
	You don't avoid the cross branding you left there.
<</if>>
<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> shivers at your touch, stealing your purity one final time. <<purity -2>><<lpurity>>
<br><br>

As soon as you're done, the bishop motions towards you. A pair of confessors grab your arms and pull you away from the altar.
"Just a precaution, dear <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>. You bear <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> taint, which makes you vulnerable." You're pulled into joining the circle.
<br><br>

The Bishop begins to chant. The confessors join in.
<br><br>

<<link [[Sing for <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> soul|Hopeless Cycle Blood Sing]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Blood Sing
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<set $tiredness to 0>>
<span class="narration">The ritual began.</span>
<br><br>

A <<worldFemale 'priestess' 'priest'>> in white robes places and lights candles around the altar. Even their flames appear red in the moonlight.
<br><br>

"<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> upon my altar, unforgiven by word," the Bishop begins, slowly raising <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> right arm.<br>
"Unforgiven by act," you and your siblings continue.<br><br>

"<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> upon my altar, who bursts with corruption,"<br>
"Like overripe fruit of sin,"<br><br>

"Hark, by Virgo, our voices heard,"<br>
"Our Mending Rite enact,"<br><br>

"Pray, put an end to the Dark Elk's seduction,"<br>
"Purge now, this filth within."<br><br>

The silk-bearers nod to each other, and quickly pull away the cloth shielding the altar.
<br><br>

As soon as the red light touches <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>, <span class="red"><<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> cries out.</span>
<br><br>

The antler erupts into a crackling rip in the air next to <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> head, as when you first saw it.
Red veins trace across <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> skin, pulsing in time with the heartbeat filling your ears.
<<if $prisoner.state is "catatonic">>
	<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> mindlessly struggles against <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> silver bindings, still unaware of <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> surroundings.
<<else>>
	<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> writhes and struggles against the silver bindings.
<</if>>
<br><br>

A few members of the flock look startled. Most are stoic. The Bishop nods to the Hand, who grows a sadistic smile and approaches with a large metal clamp.
<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> forcefully turns <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> right hand, and straps of leather join <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> restraints to force <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> hands open. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> grabs one of <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> fingers in the clamp.
<br><br>

<span class="red"><<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> screams join the song, as one of <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> fingernails is ripped out.</span>
<br><br>

<<link [[...|Hopeless Cycle Blood Choice]]>><<pass 9>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Blood Choice
<<set _thermoDisable to true>>
<span class="narration">The gaoler's choices came to a head here, in this moment.</span>
<br><br>

<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> continually struggles on the altar. The skin on <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> hands and arms blackens. Smoke hisses from where it meets silver. <<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> antler pulses and grows slightly.
<br><br>

Another fingernail. <<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> tears become black ichor running down <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> cheek.
Another. The Bishop's Hand works quickly now, as if racing against time.
<br><br>

You don't want to watch, but you can't look away. Finally, the Hand brandishes a fistful of silver needles and a hammer.
<br><br>

<<if $prisoner.state is "catatonic">>
	There's no logic, no meaning behind <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> struggles and screams. They're an automatic response from something more akin to a sick animal.
	<br><br>

	<span class="red">Because of <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> extremely poor health, there's nothing to do but watch.</span>
	<br><br>

	The hammer comes down, striking its final redemption.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Watch|Hopeless Cycle Ending D]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $prisonerEvents.includesAll("newClothes", "talkName", "talkMagic", "washHair") and ($prisonerEvents.includes("kiss") or $prisonerEvents.includesAll("sex", "virginity")) and ($prisonerEvents.includes("talkHairBlooms") or !$hcChallenge.faithBlooms)>>
	<span class="blue"><<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> hair begins to float, as if being lifted by an unfelt wind.</span>
	<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("talkHair")>>
