			<span class="purple"><<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> braid elegantly flows, the witchblooms within softly glowing.</span>
		<<else>>
			<<set $hc.witchHair to "hair-clean">>
			<span class="pink">It unbraids itself, spreading out.</span>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	The Hand appears nervous for a moment, and the flock murmurs.
	<br><br>

	<span class="green">
		<<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> hair, and intimate contact, must be key to <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> power as a witch.
	</span>
	<br><br>

	That same power seems to be hastening the spread of <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> corruption, though. The antler grows again.
	<span class="red">Something writhes under <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> skin.</span> <<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> head turns to the side to look directly at you.
	The splintering pattern on <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> forehead seems ready to burst from the other side into a second antler. <<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> mouth opens.
	<span class="red">A thin tendril flicks inside, emerging from where <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> tongue once was. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> inhales...</span>
	<br><br>

	...and says your name. Everything around you freezes in time.
	The Bishop's Hand is stopped, <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> hammer raised to strike a needle into <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> flesh.
	The confessors holding you bear no weight against you.
	The heartbeats pounding all around you go silent.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[...|Hopeless Cycle Blood Heart]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You push against the confessors holding you back, but they hold fast.
	<br><br>

	<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("washHair")>>
		<<if $hcChallenge.faithBlooms and !$prisonerEvents.includes("talkHairBlooms")>>
