			<br>
		<<else>>
			<<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> claws gleam sharply in the red moonlight, daring someone to come close.
			Your siblings rally and charge <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>.
			<br><br>

			<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> yells in pain and hatred. Your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters'>> yell out in rage and indignation. A flurry of sharp claws meet them.
			<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> holds <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> own at first, but the storm of whips and the sheer number of your siblings overwhelm <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>.
			<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>>'s beaten and restrained after much blood is spilled. <span class="red"><<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> never stood a chance alone.</span>
			<br><br>

			<<link [[Too late|Hopeless Cycle Ending B]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Hopeless Cycle Ending F [ending]
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<canvas-model-override "mouth" "neutral">>
<span class="narration">
	This is the simplest version of the story, almost a fable. Needless to say, very little is accepted as fact.
	<br><br>

	Through <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> mistreatment, the witch...
</span>
<br><br>

<<if $phase is 1>>
	You and the Bishop's Hand enter the cell with the confessor, and you all freeze.
<<else>>
	You enter the cell, and freeze.
<</if>>
From the tiny barred window, a flood of grass, leaves and algae have spilled into the cell. The forest has invaded. It grows to the far wall, where it circles into a maw of thorns.
<br><br>

<span class="narration">...shed <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> mortal flesh.</span>
<br><br>

<<if ($settings.npcPregnancyEnabled or $settings.nnpcPregnancyEnabled) and $prisonerEvents.includesAny("raped", "elkspawnEmbrace", "sex")>>
	<<print $prisoner.name.toUpperFirst()>>'s shackles are gone. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>>'s curled up on the floor around something.
	<<if $prisoner.love gte 40>>
		You run to <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> side and turn <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> over.
	<<else>>
		You walk to <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> side and push <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> over with your foot.
	<</if>>
	You hear a short whine, and some babbling.
	<br><br>

	<span class="red"><<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>>'s holding a baby.</span>
	<br><br>

	You try to shake <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> awake. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> doesn't move. The baby looks to you, their hand in their mouth.
	<br><br>

	It shouldn't be possible. It's only been days, and <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> showed no signs of bearing child.
	<<if $prisonerEvents.includesAny("elkspawnEmbrace", "sex")>>
		Could this really be the result of your brief union?
	<<else>>
		Could this really be the result of <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> violation at the hands of one of your <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters'>>?
	<</if>>
	You reach down.
	<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("talkHairBlooms")>>
		<span class="purple">The blooms you braided into <<= $prisoner.name>>'s hair are bound to their arm.</span>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	The baby's eyes glow in the dim light. Your joints become stiff and unresponsive. <span class="red">You can't move! Its jaws split and open wide, like that of a snake. It bites your hand, before lunging at you. Your screams are swiftly silenced.</span>
	<br><br>

	<span class="narration">
		And, through <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> terrible serpent offspring, <<print $prisoner.name>> had <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> revenge.
		But it wasn't enough. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> needed more. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> needed to make all of the faithful pay in blood.
		So great was <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> anger, <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> vengeance, <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> hunger, that this abhorrent child was not truly <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> progeny.
		<br><br>

		It was <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>, given new flesh. Mutual hatred turned <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> into a living curse. For years, the cloister would try to hunt <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> down.
		Sometimes they were successful, only for <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> to be reborn yet again, all the more hateful.
	</span>
<<else>>
	<<print $prisoner.name.toUpperFirst()>> is gone. In <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> place are piled, thick scraps of something translucent and scaly.
	You approach and kneel down. It looks like the shed husk of a snake. It crumbles at your touch.
	<br><br>

	You were mistaken. The forest didn't grow into the cell. It sprouted out, from right here. The stone is cracked.
	<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("talkHairBlooms")>>
		<span class="purple">The flowers you braided into <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> hair have taken root and become overgrown.</span>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<span class="narration">
		But, as the story goes, <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> was not truly gone. This version claims that <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> lived on as a great serpent.
		A creature of purest sin, to exact <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> revenge on the faithful. A living curse born of mutual hatred.
	</span>
	<br><br>

	You hear a faint slithering. From the shadows, a pair of piercing yellow eyes glare at you. Your joints become stiff and unresponsive. <span class="red">You can't move!</span>
	The jaws of sin split open, and lunge for you.
	<br><br>

	<span class="narration">For years, the cloister would try to hunt <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> down. Sometimes they were successful, only for <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> to be reborn yet again, all the more hateful.</span>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<span class="narration">
	Unable to find peace, this brutal conflict drew on for centuries. The cloister, in their eyes, were vindicated.
	They were right to persecute, to punish, as the unholy were capable of becoming monsters that could haunt them for generations to come.
	<br><br>

	Thus, the Hopeless Cycle of <span class="red">Hatred</span> repeats.
</span>
<<set $hc.ending to "F">>
<br><br>

<<link [[The serpent devours itself|Hopeless Cycle End]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Ending E [ending]
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<set $location to "old_temple">>
<<set $hcItems to []>><<canvas-model-override "mouth" "neutral">><<set $pain to 15>>
<<strip>><<upperwear "rag top">><<lowerwear "rag skirt">><<legswear "gold anklets">>
<span class="narration">In this version of the story, paranoia led the gaoler to become a prisoner <<worldMale 'himself' 'herself'>>.</span>
<br><br>

You awaken with a splitting headache. You try to move, but your legs pull against something. You open your eyes.
<br><br>

Your legs are bound, and you've been dressed in rags. There's a lit torch in a sconce. <span class="red">You're in <<= $prisoner.name>>'s cell, bound to the wall opposite <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>.</span>
<<if $prisoner.harmed gte Math.floor($prisoner.love / 6)>>
	<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> glares at you, but seems to be restraining <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> anger. You're on equal ground now.
<<elseif $prisoner.love gte 60>>
	<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> sadly smiles at you.
<<else>>
	<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> stares at you.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<span class="narration">How quickly the faithful turned on their sibling. How eager they were to think the worst.</span>
<br><br>

<<generateConfessor 1>><<person1>>
You pull on your shackles, causing them to rattle. A confessor appears at the door shortly after.
"<<worldMale 'Brother' 'Sister'>>. I am sorry, but you are tainted. Bewitched. You will remain here until the witch is cleansed."
<br><br>

<<if $player.virginity.penile isnot true>>
	<<He>> pauses for a moment, before scowling. "You will also join in on <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> punishments, as you have failed your chastity examination."
	<br><br>
<</if>>

You slump back against the wall, resigned to your fate. You know there's no escaping. You know it better than anyone.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Ending E 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Ending E 2 [ending]
<<set _thermoDisable to true>>
<<canvas-model-override "mouth" "neutral">><<set $trauma to 5000>>
<<run Time.timeTravel(new DateTime(1390, 5, 31, 22, 0))>>
<<set Weather.set("clear", true, 1000)>>
<span class="narration">
	They made <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> wait until the night of the ritual, and then... nothing.
	<br><br>

	They took the witch away, and conducted the ritual without <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> never returned.
	<br><br>

	The following day, <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> faced penance and returned to <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> duties, but <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> was never the same. Something was missing.
	<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> felt as though <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> lacked true purpose. <<worldMale 'His' 'Her'>> requests to know what happened to the witch were met with silence,
	the same maddening silence that now filled the dungeon. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> came to hate that silence.
	<br><br>

	Meanwhile, the cloister's persecution turned inwards. Following the ritual, a haze fell over the flock.
	It started when they were given direct orders by the Hand to never tell the gaoler what had happened that night.
	The veil of secrecy led to rumours and lies spreading and to be accepted as fact, and before long,
	hysteria led them to believe the witch was still here, <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> spirit possessing someone.
	<<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> visage creeped in shadowed corners, <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> hateful eye visible at the feet of beds.
	<br><br>

	The gaoler soon realised that <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> siblings were all in on the secret, speaking only in hushed whispers around <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>.
	<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> became isolated and obsessive, which only led <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> siblings to alienate <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> further.
	<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("talkHairBlooms")>>
		It all came to a head when <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> discovered a pair of flowers in <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> bed. The same flowers <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> had braided into <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> hair. It made <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> snap.
	<<else>>
		It drove <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> to insanity. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> began to demand answers, <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> anger and paranoia ruling over <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>, until one day... <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> snapped.
	<</if>>
	<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> cursed all of <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> siblings one last time, before flying into a frenzy.
	<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> was eventually restrained, but only after injuring dozens. They say <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> fought as though possessed.
	<br><br>

	Indeed, they now had their scapegoat. Everything was blamed on the gaoler, supposedly possessed by the witch.
	<<worldMale 'His' 'Her'>> siblings saw <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> hatred in <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> eyes, and heard <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> cackle on <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> lips.
	Unfortunately for them, they might have been correct.
	Now whole of body, the dungeon would not hold the two of them a second time. They escaped as one entity, and fled.
	<br><br>

	<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> would begin a crusade of vengeance that some say lasts to this day,
	as <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> continually feeds on the uncertainty and doubt of the faithful, driving them to question and alienate their siblings
	until <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> can worm <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> way into their bodies, shedding <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> old flesh like a snake sheds its skin.
	<br><br>

	Thus, the Hopeless Cycle of <span class="pink">Paranoia</span> repeats.
</span>
<<set $hc.ending to "E">>
<br><br>

<<link [[Ignorance, bliss|Hopeless Cycle End]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Ending D [ending]
<<set _thermoDisable to true>>
<<canvas-model-override "mouth" "neutral">><<canvas-model-override "eyes_half" true>>
<<canvas-model-override "arm_left" "none">><<canvas-model-override "arm_right" "none">>
<<hopelessCycleBrandings>>

<<set $follower to {
	name: "witchprisoner",
	base: "base",
	left_arm: "left-arm",
	hair: $hc.witchHair,
	writing_right_cheek: _brandings.right_cheek,
	writing_chest: _brandings.chest,
	writing_left_arm: _brandings.left_arm,
	writing_right_arm: _brandings.right_arm,
	writing_right_shoulder: _brandings.right_shoulder,
	writing_right_thigh: _brandings.right_thigh,
	writing_right_leg: _brandings.right_leg,
	writing_right_foot: _brandings.right_foot
}>>
<span class="narration">In this version of the tale, the gaoler didn't attempt to stop the ritual. The needles of judgement found their mark.</span>
<br><br>

<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> doesn't move anymore. Countless needles pierce <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> flesh, embedded within. The Hand looks down, bored by <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> lack of response.
<br><br>

<<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> eyes are vacant and empty. If not for the gentle rise and fall of <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> chest, you'd think the worst.
<br><br>

"<<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> vessel is sealed, and <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> is forgiven," the Bishop says. "The corruption will not escape <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> will bear it until it fades."
<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> turns to you. "You will continue to watch over <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> until <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> is empty."
<br><br>

The confessors release you. You walk to <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> side, and lift <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> up.
<br><br>

You feel numb.
<br><br>

<<link [[Go home|Hopeless Cycle Ending D 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Ending D 2 [ending]
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<set $location to "lake">>
<<run Time.timeTravel(new DateTime(1390, 11, 30, 21, 30))>>
<<set Weather.Temperature.set(-25)>>
<<set Weather.set("heavyPrecipitation", true)>>
<<set V.weatherObj.snow = (80)>>
<<set $trauma to 5000>>
<span class="narration">
	The witch would never move again. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> lay in <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> cell, slumped over like an unwanted doll cast aside.
	No matter what twisted punishment the Hand devised, <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> never reacted.
	<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("spendNight")>>
		The gaoler spent most of <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> nights in <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> cell, sleeping next to <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>.
	<<else>>
		The gaoler began to visit <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> cell more than ever.
	<</if>>
	To <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> siblings, <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> appeared obsessive.
	<br><br>

	<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> claimed <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> was now speaking to <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>, which, of course, raised eyebrows.
	<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> told <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> that <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> body had finally failed due to the trauma of the ritual.
	<<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> mind was trapped inside. <<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> only reprieve came from skinship with <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>.
	Otherwise, <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> was stuck watching the world from that unmoving, unblinking grey eye.
	<br><br>

	Soon, the gaoler stopped speaking to anyone but <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>.
	The last thing <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> said to <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> siblings sent chills throughout the whole flock:
	'<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> only wants a new body. We owe it to <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>.'
	<br><br>

	Months passed. The 'taint' within <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> never faded. It stayed in <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> body, stagnant and rotting along with it. At the end of each month, <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> was brought to the altar again, and the flock would sing for <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>, begging God to purify <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> body and soul.
	No blood was ever enough to bring <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> back, though.
	<<if $settings.npcPregnancyEnabled or $settings.nnpcPregnancyEnabled>>
		<br><br>

		The punishments would finally grind to a halt when <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> began to show signs of being with child.
		<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("sex")>>
			The love the two shared before the first ritual had borne fruit.
		<<elseif $prisonerEvents.includes("elkspawnEmbrace")>>
			The defilement that the witch had visited upon the gaoler had borne fruit.
		<<elseif $prisonerEvents.includes("rape")>>
			The <<worldMale 'monk' 'nun'>> that assaulted <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> had impregnated <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>.
		<<else>>
			The implications were unpleasant. Most suspected the gaoler of defiling <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> in <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> catatonic state.
		<</if>>
		<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> was kept sheltered, the gaoler still taking care of <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> all the while.
		Thanks to <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> obsessive care, and despite <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> broken body, <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> would carry the child to term... but <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> body would not survive the ordeal.
		<<if !$prisonerEvents.includes("rape")>>
			None who saw the child doubted that the gaoler was the <<worldMale 'father' 'mother'>>. The resemblance was obvious. <<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> would never face punishment, though.
		<<else>>
			The <<worldMale 'monk' 'nun'>> responsible was found and punished accordingly.
		<</if>>
		The gaoler would abandon <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> faith, fleeing the temple and leaving the infant in the care of <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> <<worldMale 'brothers' 'sisters'>>.
	<<else>>
		One night, the gaoler was seen walking into the forest, alone. The witch had simply vanished from <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> cell, too.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	The monthly rituals instead became a monthly vigil. For years the flock searched for their missing <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>, but would never find <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>.
	Even though they could hear <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> and <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> beloved witch laughing in the red moonlight.
	<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("talkHairBlooms")>>
		Even though they found a familiar pair of flowers out in the forest, the same flowers that the gaoler had braided into <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> hair.
	<</if>>
	Even though some claimed to see them dancing on the lake shore, the witch finally whole of body, before both flickering out of existence.
	<br><br>

	The temple would finally accept that their souls were happy, and had found rest. At least, that's what they said to the public.
	In reality, the gaoler's remark of the witch needing a new body made the cloister jumpy.
	These events would repeat themselves with disturbing similarity, time and time again, whenever they suspected someone of being inhabited by the soul of the witch.
	The altar's thirst for blood could not be quenched. They feared <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> influence, feared that <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> would steal more of their siblings away.
	<br><br>

	Thus, the Hopeless Cycle of <span class="purple">Stagnation</span> repeats.
</span>
<<set $hc.ending to "D">>
<br><br>

<<link [[Rest for the wicked|Hopeless Cycle End]]>><<unset $follower>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Ending C [ending]
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<canvas-model-override "mouth" "neutral">><<wearProp "whip" "khaki">>
<span class="narration">In this version of the tale, the gaoler, the houndmaster, let the beast loose on <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> who had defiled <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>. This was what <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> deemed to be justice.</span>
<br><br>

You release <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> leash. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> cries out in rage as <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> lunges. <<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> claw pierces <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> flesh.
<br><br>

You watch as <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> gives back every last drop of defilement that <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> inflicted upon <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> is not gentle. You know <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> won't kill <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>, though. A broken vessel holds nothing.
<br><br>

Blood runs down <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> arms, and a black ichor flows from <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> hateful eye. The antler gradually recedes, the world mending around it. Each time <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> dares to raise a hand against <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>, you whip <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>> until <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> submits again.
<br><br>

The Bishop's Hand watches closely, <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> hands gripping the bars of the door. <<worldMale 'His' 'Her'>> ugly features are awash with fascination.
<br><br>

You tune out the defiler's screams easily enough. It's rarely quiet in the temple's dungeon.
<br><br>

<<link [[Punish|Hopeless Cycle Ending C 2]]>><<pass 120>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Ending C 2 [ending]
<<set _thermoDisable to true>>
<span class="narration">The <<worldMale 'monk' 'nun'>> was broken. The gaoler grinned. This was <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> punishment. This was deserved. This was everything the cloister stood for.</span>
<br><br>

For hours, <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> ravages <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>. The crosses on the walls glow. <<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> thigh bruises have grown from the strain. <<worldFemale 'Her' 'His'>> voice lets out low, satisfied breaths rather than screams of anger.
<br><br>

<span class="pink"><<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> shudders in climax one final time.</span> <span class="red">The <<worldMale 'monk' 'nun'>> lays limp, <<worldMale 'his' 'her'>> eyes blank.</span>
<br><br>

The door to the cell creaks open, and you pull the silk cord. <<print $prisoner.name.toUpperFirst()>> obediently crawls away from the <<worldMale 'monk' 'nun'>>, allowing the confessors to retrieve <<worldMale 'him' 'her'>>. "You're contaminated, <<worldMale 'brother' 'sister'>>. You must be purified."
<br><br>

<<worldMale 'He' 'She'>> will be punished, for being punished. Just as <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> had been. Your grip on the leash slackens, the tension in your body fading. This was immaculate justice. <<print $prisoner.name.toUpperFirst()>> lies at your feet.
You sit down and cautiously lower your hand, petting <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> on the head. You expect the familiar feeling of cold weakness to spread through you when you make contact, but it's absent. <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> must have given it all to <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> victim.
<br><br>

"<<worldMale 'Brother' 'Sister'>>," the Hand's voice snaps you back to attention. "Forget your previous orders. You are no longer this witch's guard. We have uses for <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>. You are to be <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> keeper, instead."
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Hopeless Cycle Ending C 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Hopeless Cycle Ending C 3 [ending]
<<set _thermoDisable to true>>
<<run Time.timeTravel(new DateTime(1390, 8, 3, 12, 30))>>
<<set Weather.set("heavyPrecipitation", true, 600)>>
<<set $trauma to 5000>><<set $stress to 0>><<set $control to 1000>><<set $purity to 500>><<set $arousal to 7000>><<set $pleasure to 5000>>
<<set $player.virginity.penile to $prisoner.name>><<set $player.virginity.temple to false>>
<<canvas-model-override "arm_left" "none">><<canvas-model-override "arm_right" "none">>
<<set _witchClothes to $hcItems.find(clothes => clothes.type is "clothes" and clothes.location is "prisoner")?.name>>
<<hopelessCycleBrandings>>

<<if $prisonerEvents.includes("talkHairBlooms")>>
	<<set $hc.witchHair to "hair-flowers">>
<<elseif $prisonerEvents.includes("talkHair")>>
	<<set $hc.witchHair to "hair-braid">>
<<elseif $prisonerEvents.includes("washHair")>>
	<<set $hc.witchHair to "hair-clean">>
<<else>>
	<<set $hc.witchHair to "hair-dirty">>
<</if>>

<<if $prisoner.bandagesOn>>
	<<set _bandages to "bandages-alt">>
<</if>>
<<if _witchClothes is "robe">>
	<<set _clothes to "robe-alt">>
<<elseif _witchClothes is "bloodstained sack" or _witchClothes is "torn vegetable sack">>
	<<set _clothes to "sack-alt">>
<</if>>
<<if _brandings.chest>>
	<<set _brandings.chest to "brand-chest-alt">>
<</if>>
<<if _brandings.right_arm>>
	<<set _brandings.right_arm to "brand-right-arm-alt">>
<</if>>

<<set $follower to {
	name: "witchprisoner",
	base: "base-alt",
	left_arm: "left-arm-alt",
	clothes: _clothes,
	under_clothes: _bandages,
	hair: $hc.witchHair,
	writing_right_cheek: _brandings.right_cheek,
	writing_chest: _brandings.chest,
	writing_right_arm: _brandings.right_arm,
	writing_right_shoulder: _brandings.right_shoulder,
	writing_right_thigh: _brandings.right_thigh,
	writing_right_leg: _brandings.right_leg,
	writing_right_foot: _brandings.right_foot
}>>
<span class="narration">
