	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		"I had hoped one version might be kinder," you say. "Though I suppose stories like this rarely are."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
		"Is every version of this story such a downer?" You fold your arms, trying not to look as affected as you feel.
	<<else>>
		"Usually fairy tales have a happy ending." You try to make it sound like an observation, not a complaint.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	Winter allows <<himself>> to chuckle. "Well, I've been excluding one version of the story. I wished to see how invested you were.
	Now that you've gone and exhausted every other version of it, I think you've earned it. <span class="gold">Next time, I'll tell you some missing details when we begin.</span>"
	<br><br>

	<<He>> clears <<his>> throat. "Next time. You're good at letting me talk until I lose my voice."
<<else>>
	"That's only one version of the story. There are many more." Winter stands up from <<his>> seat and stretches.
	<br><br>

	"Unfortunately, my voice grows weary. I'll be happy to tell you a different version next time."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<set $hcEndings.pushUnique(_endingSeen)>>
<<hopelessCycleEndings>>
<<if _endingSeen is "S">>
	<<specialClothesUnlock "set" "chain_tunic">>
<</if>>
<<set $museumAntiques.paintings.paintingsnake to "museum">>

<<link [[Next|Museum]]>><<unset $hcChallenge>><<endevent>><</link>>
